BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Social Contractors – Live & Free @ Twin Oaks Roadhouse!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T160000
UID:260922qi-eM32Qs0OgbqLZojW-oQ
DESCRIPTION:***“….Get ready for the super-entertaining sounds of local
  band The Social Contractors. They totally rock\, in all the right ways…
 ”*** - Argus-Courier\n\nJoin The Social Contractors at Twin Oaks Roadhou
 se for a lively afternoon of upbeat original rock plus their own spin on c
 lassic hits you know and love (e.g. Beatles\, CCR\, Hendrix\, Doors\, Pink
  Floyd\, Police\, Men At Work\, U2\, Tears for Fears\, Tom Petty\, Steely 
 Dan\, Foreigner\, Steve Miller\, and more)!\n\nWhether you enjoy melodic v
 ocals\, searing guitar and sax solos\, intriguing lyrics\, captivating son
 gs\, or just great dynamic and danceable rhythms\, The Social Contractors 
 always deliver and never disappoint!\n\nThe lineup for this free live perf
 ormance features band founder and songwriter\, Jason E Davies (lead vocals
 \, lead/rhythm guitar)\, Travis Thayer (sax/keys/vocals)\, Rob Neidel (bas
 s/vocals)\, and Chris Oatman (drums).\n\nAbout Twin Oaks Roadhouse: Charm 
 and character have accumulated at this very spot since 1926\, making the T
 win Oaks a place where stories are told and made. Whatever your definition
  of a tavern\, honky tonk or roadhouse\, rest assured there’s a bit of e
 ach in here. Take a break travelers. There’s a bar\, a fireplace\, a kit
 chen\, a backyard and a dance floor.
LOCATION:Twin Oaks Roadhouse
URL:https://www.sonomacounty.com/food-drink/restaurants/twin-oaks-roadhous
 e/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:UC Master Gardeners Fall Faire
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T160000
UID:260922i0Vby6mf-EueawrDll8HZQ
DESCRIPTION:The UC Master Gardeners Fall Faire is a free\, lively\, all ag
 es event from 1-4pm on Saturday\, September 26\, with over 30 educational 
 and community partner exhibits and hands-on demonstrations\, Scarecrow Row
 \, an ornamental & winter veggie plant sale\, special activities for kids\
 , including books\, and so much more!   \n\nLearn how to dehydrate summe
 r’s bounty\, create garlands from your garden\, take succulent clippings
 \, swap seeds and get seeds\, ask garden questions at our Help Desk.  Hon
 e your tool sharpening skills\, explore the Japanese Art of Bonsai and the
  Napa Valley Orchid Society\, go native with the CA Native Plant Society\,
  learn about bees & bugs\, Firewise landscaping\, roses\, healthy soils\, 
 growing veggies year-round\, and more.\n\nAnnie's Lunch Box food truck and
  the Big Ranch Rounders will offer food and entertainment. \n\nJoin us for
  this fun\, fall Faire!\n\nLocation: UC Master Gardeners of Napa County\, 
 1710 Soscol Avenue\, Napa \\(near Central Valley Hardware\\)\n\nDate/Time:
  Saturday\, September 26\, 1-4pm.
LOCATION:UC Master Gardeners of Napa County
URL:https://ucanr.edu/site/uc-master-gardeners-napa-county/event/napa-coun
 ty-master-gardeners-fall-faire
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Qi Gong at Barbieri Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T110000
UID:260920UTIgqI7rRU6IenWnBZSkBg
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an hour of movement. Qi Gong \\(pronounced "chee g
 ong"\\) is a gentle practice of movement\, breathing\, intention and mindf
 ulness. Think of it as meditation in motion. The movements are simple and 
 easy to learn. Everything can be adapted for a variety of abilities. All a
 re welcome...no experience necessary. You'll leave class feeling less stre
 ss and more of your inner vitality. Classes taughy by Marianne Benforado i
 s a licensed acupuncturist and certified Holden Qi Gong teacher. Students 
 describe her classes as welcoming and down to earth with good vibes sprink
 led on top. Drop in anytime it works for your schedule.
LOCATION:Barbieri Park in Healdsburg (Parkland Farms)
URL:https://feelbetteracu.com/events/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
