BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ink & Rhythm
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T180000
UID:260917iSaoQiCeW0SyydhQ44EvbA
DESCRIPTION:A Live Performance Celebrating Creativity\, Memory & Cultural 
 Connection\n\nExperience an extraordinary collaboration between acclaimed 
 Chinese American artist Jun Jun and internationally celebrated Zimbabwean 
 musician Piwai\, as painting and music unfold together in a live performan
 ce exploring creativity\, memory\, and cultural connection.\n\nThroughout 
 the evening\, Jun Jun will create expressive paintings in real time while 
 Piwai responds through song\, mbira\, and rhythm\, weaving together two ar
 tistic traditions in an improvisational dialogue that transcends language.
  Together\, they invite audiences to experience how art can carry memory\,
  celebrate identity\, and build bridges across cultures.\n\nFollowing the 
 performance\, meet the artists\, explore the exhibition\, and enjoy authen
 tic Zimbabwean cuisine provided by the Zimbabwe Cultural Exchange Project 
 of California.
LOCATION:Petaluma Museum
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/ink-rhythm-tickets-1997155896047?aff=ebds
 oporgprofile
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Memoir Writing Workshop for Women: Crafting Your Life Story
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T170000
UID:260917gBrMTD50MECBQAeVn_nImQ
DESCRIPTION:Transform Your Memories into Meaningful Narrative\n\nA Writing
  Retreat in Beautiful West County\n\nReady to tell your story? Your memori
 es are waiting to become literature. Discover the power of your personal s
 tory and learn to craft it with authenticity\, depth\, and literary grace.
 \n\nWorkshop Overview\n\nJoin us for an immersive memoir writing experienc
 e designed to help you uncover\, shape\, and share the stories that have d
 efined your life. Whether you're a complete beginner or have been writing 
 for years\, this workshop will provide you with the tools and confidence t
 o transform your memories into compelling prose.\n\nWhat You will Learn:\n
 \nMemory Mining Techniques\n\nNarrative Structure\n\nVoice & Perspective\n
 \nScene Construction\n\nTruth vs. Accuracy\n\nCharacter Development\n\nRev
 ision Strategies\n\nDetails\n\nWorkshop fee is $147\, $127 for OCA members
 . Limited to 8 participants. Held in the OCA Studio.\n\nLed By\n\nAlaura O
 ’Dell (MFA)\, an experienced memoir author and writing instructor.
LOCATION:Occidental Center for the Arts
URL:https://eventvesta.com/events/163611/t/tickets
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:"Caribbean Cocktails" Book Release
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T200000
UID:260917T8zKYQIPSUaC3EcGkGKhKw
DESCRIPTION:**PREMO Club Presents "Caribbean Cocktails" Book Release + Soc
 ial Mixer**\n\nYou are invited to join us for an exclusive experience in t
 he heart of Sonoma's wine country to celebrate the upcoming book release 
 ***"Caribbean Cocktails: Drinks & Bites from the Afro-Latino Diaspora"***\
 , (June 2\, 2026 from Ten Speed Press). The book is authored by chef and c
 ocktail creator **Nelson German** and James Beard Award–winning culina
 ry writer **Andréa Lawson Gray**.\n\nHosted at **Aldina Vineyard's Tast
 ing Lounge**\,\n\nThe evening begins at 5pm with a cocktail + wine recepti
 on featuring herbs\, fruits\, and botanicals grown at Little Saint Farm hi
 ghlighting the farm’s seasonal produce. The evening concludes with an au
 thor talk.\n\nThis event is not only a culinary affair\, but also will rai
 se funds for **Sprouts Chef Training**\, a Bay area-based 501(c)(3) nonpr
 ofit helping under-resourced youth build careers in the culinary industry.
  Through culinary training\, mentorship\, and job placement support\, Spro
 uts equips youth to rise from hardship through culinary training and job p
 lacement. Graduates use these entry-level jobs to kickstart culinary caree
 rs\, pay for education\, or pursue new industries.\n\nVisit **https://pre
 moclub.com/events** for more information.
LOCATION:Bacchus Landing
URL:https://premoclub.com/events/caribbean-cocktails-book-release
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:On Site Compost and Biochar Demonstration
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T130000
UID:260917QxqlZxnTUkm9QG_i5PA8Fg
DESCRIPTION:Please join us for the first in a series of composti
 ng workshops taught by Bobby Nicholson of Compost Depot with the
  Sonoma Ecology Center \\(SEC\\) and Sonoma Biochar Initiative \\
 (SBI\\). The workshops are funded by Zero Waste Sonoma \\(ZWS\\)
  and free to the public. The workshop series will continue with
  five on site compost workshops throughout Sonoma county. \n\nLet
 's get dirty! The workshop will provide practical guidelines and
  accessible soil science to build a healthy composting program o
 n location with available resources and using a scalable model. 
 Raymond Baltar of SBI will introduce the basics and science of 
 biochar\, including use of the flame cap kiln\, and demonstrate 
 the integration of biochar into a compost program.This will be a
  handson learning opportunity for agricultural producers of all s
 izes\, and at the end of the workshop\, attendees will have the
  resources and know-how to build a composting program on-site. T
 he workshops will be bilingual\, taught in English and Spanish.\n
 \nLe invitamos a participar en el primero de una serie de talle
 res sobre compostaje impartidos por Bobby Nicholson\, de Compost 
 Depot\, en colaboración con el Sonoma Ecology Center \\(SEC\\) y
  la Sonoma Biochar Initiative \\(SBI\\). Estos talleres cuentan c
 on el financiamiento de Zero Waste Sonoma \\(ZWS\\) y son gratui
 tos para el público.\n\n¡Manos a la obra! El taller ofrecerá 
 pautas prácticas y nociones accesibles de ciencia del suelo para
  establecer un programa de compostaje saludable en el propio lug
 ar de trabajo\, utilizando recursos disponibles y un modelo escal
 able. Raymond Baltar\, de la SBI\, presentará los fundamentos y
  la ciencia del biocarbón —incluyendo el uso del horno de ti
 po "flame cap" kiln— y demostrará cómo integrar este material
  en un programa de compostaje. \n\nSerá una oportunidad de apre
 ndizaje práctico para agricultores\, productores agrícolas\, encar
 gados de jardines o invernaderos y paisajistas de cualquier escal
 a. Al finalizar el taller\, los asistentes contarán con los rec
 ursos y los conocimientos necesarios para implementar un programa
  de compostaje en sus propias instalaciones. Los talleres serán
  bilingües \\(impartidos en inglés y español\\).\n\nFecha: Sába
 do\, 26 de septiembre de 2026\; de 10:00 a. m. a 1:00 p. m.\n
 \nLugar: Sonoma Garden Park\, 19996 7th St E\, Sonoma\, CA 95476
 \n\nDirigido a: Agricultores\, productores agrícolas\, encargados d
 e jardines o invernaderos y paisajísticas del condado de Sonoma.
LOCATION:Sonoma Garden Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/zero-compost-workshop
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
