DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T200000
UID:260914ivBF5IHPVkm_v1AsnCQJ-w
DESCRIPTION:Born and raised in the small town of Canton\, South Dakota\, T
 yler Halverson brings a fresh\, unfiltered voice to modern country music. 
 Blending classic country and western influences with a rock-and-roll spiri
 t\, sharp songwriting\, and stories shaped by life on the road\, Halverson
  creates music for cowboys\, hippies\, drifters\, and everyone in between.
  Following his Grand Ole Opry debut and the release of his deeply honest a
 lbum In Defense of Drinking\, he brings his unmistakable sound to the Mys
 tic Theatre on Saturday\, September 26.\n\nhttps://www.tylerhalverson.com/
 \n\nOpening the show is - Ben Garcia\n\nhttps://bengarciamusic.com/\n\nBor
 n on the Wasatch Front and raised at the foot of the Rockies\, Ben Garcia 
 got his musical start with early success in the alternative rock scene. Ye
 t\, after years on long Western highways—often with only bird dogs\, hor
 ses\, and a Gibson Guitar as companions—his music picked up grit from mo
 untain passes and country roads. His songs drive through sometimes stark\,
  sometimes sublime landscapes towards a jagged but unbroken skyline\, stop
 ping occasionally at Honky Tonk bars to tell stories of rough\, worn cowbo
 y hats\, boots\, and tales lov
LOCATION:Mystic Theatre & Music Hall
URL:https://wl.eventim.us/event/tyler-halverson/703317?afflky=MysticTheatr
 e2
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Plein Air Watercolor Landscapes with Built Structures
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T150000
UID:260914i6P8KgptpEGxtEOTpMeUrg
DESCRIPTION:Presented in partnership with the Sonoma Community Center\, pa
 rticipants will explore both watercolor technique and the core principles 
 of landscape painting\, including composition\, color temperature\, and at
 mospheric perspective. Artist Hannah Day will guide participtants to creat
 e movement and depth in a painting and gain a new appreciation for the bea
 uty of the surroundings through the process of close observation and caref
 ul rendering.\n\nThe class begins with quick thumbnail sketches\, then eac
 h person selects one composition to focus on throughout the day. Through d
 emonstration and individual instruction\, they learn color mixing and wate
 rcolor techniques while building their painting step by step.  All levels
  of experience are welcome.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/events/plein-air-watercolor-landscapes-sept
 ember-2026/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
