UID:260823xSqi6QzBG02CQc9pL-HlRg
DESCRIPTION:Saturday & Sunday\n\nDate & Time\n\nSeptember 26 · 10:00 AM 
 – 5:00 PM\n\nSeptember 27 · 10:00 AM – 4:00 PM\n\nLocation\n\nRoom 11
 0\n\nCategory\n\nEvents\, Fiber Arts\, Other\n\nExperience Level\n\nAll Le
 vels\n\nAges\n\n18 and older\n\nOne Day Registration:\n\n$30\n\nFull Weeke
 nd Registration:\n\n$60\n\nTotal Registration Cost:\n\n$30 – $60\n\nJoin
  artist and educator\, Valerie Seaberg for a two-day immersive lantern-bui
 lding workshop inspired by Día de los Muertos\, ancestral remembrance\, a
 nd joy of creating in community. Together we will create illuminated lante
 rn sculptures that honor loved ones\, celebrate lineage from all cultures 
 and traditions\, and welcome the deepening beauty of fall and winter. Usin
 g willow\, bamboo\, reed\, paper\, and other sustainable materials\, parti
 cipants will learn how to build expressive sculptural lanterns from the in
 side out. Participants are encouraged to bring ideas\, sketches\, photogra
 phs\, symbols\, or meaningful inspiration connected to ancestors\, memory\
 , nature\, or personal vision. Lanterns may be abstract\, playful\, elegan
 t\, symbolic\, animal-inspired\, or devotional in form. This workshop is o
 pen to beginners as well as experienced makers.Together we will create a c
 elebration of light honoring those who came before us and illuminating the
  path forward.\n\nRequired Supply List\n\nPlease bring the following suppl
 ies to the class:\n\nPruning Shears\n\nSketchbook\n\nOptional: Meaningful 
 images\, poems\, or small materials to inspire your design
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/fall-lantern-workshop-weeke
 nd-workshop/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Introduction to Reduction Linocut
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T130000
UID:260823a16ltzKeP0OQ3gm6eP1BzA
DESCRIPTION:Saturdays Weekly · 4 Weeks\n\nDate & Time\n\nSeptember 5 – 
 26\, 2026\n\n10:00 AM – 1:00 PM\n\nLocation\n\nRoom 208\n\nCategory\n\nP
 rintmaking\n\nExperience Level\n\nBeginning\n\nAges\n\n18 and older\n\nReg
 istration Cost:\n\n$195\n\nMaterials Fee:\n\n$30\n\nTotal Registration Cos
 t:\n\n$225\n\nIn this special four-week workshop\, participants will explo
 re the unique art of reduction relief printmaking. Acclaimed guest artist\
 , Tomoko Murakami\, will demonstrate how to create multi-color prints from
  a single linoleum block. The main idea is to gradually carve away parts o
 f the block and print each new layer of color\, with each layer building o
 n the previous one. The course covers the entire process\, from designing 
 and planning\, to carving techniques\, inking\, registration\, and printin
 g with both hand and printing press methods. Participants will learn to ex
 plore the possibilities of color mixing and layering\, enabling students t
 o achieve intricate designs and a wide range of visual effects. You will g
 ain an understanding of the materials\, processes\, and innovations involv
 ed in this unique form of relief print printing!All levels are welcome\, i
 ncluding continuing linocut students. Please note: This class requires ha
 nd dexterity to maneuver the carving tool. Participants should feel comfor
 table standing\, and using tools with sharp blades and edges.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/introduction-to-reduction-l
 inocut/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
