BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sonoma Valley of the Moon Vintage Festival
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T000000
UID:260918qtCl3pA0FEy9jVwD3IH1DA
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate Sonoma Valley's rich winemaking heritage at the  Val
 ley of the Moon Vintage Festival \, taking place September 24-27\, 2026. T
 his beloved community celebration features Sonoma Valley wines\, local foo
 d\, live music\, and family-friendly activities throughout the historic So
 noma Plaza.Highlights include the traditional Grape Stomp\, Blessing of th
 e Grapes\, live music\, a Wine Garden\, artisan fair\, kids' activities\, 
 and the Sonoma Valley Grand Tasting featuring wines from more than 40 wine
 ries. Special experiences throughout the weekend include a Harvest Immersi
 on\, Harvest Dinner\, and Brunch Bites & Bubbles. The 2026 festival celebr
 ates the 200th Anniversary of Sonoma Valley Wine with the theme "Year of C
 ommunity\," bringing locals and visitors together to celebrate harvest\, h
 istory\, wine\, and community.
LOCATION:Various Sonoma County Locations
URL:https://www.sonoma.com/event/the-valley-of-the-moon-vintage-festival/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:River & Redwoods Film Festival
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T000000
UID:260713OwfmGGQp0EuI_yME9QeNrw
DESCRIPTION:The River & Redwoods Film Festival returns to Monte Rio for a 
 special weekend celebrating independent film\, creativity\, community\, an
 d the natural beauty of Northern California. Set among the towering redwoo
 ds and along the banks of the Russian River\, the festival brings filmmake
 rs\, film lovers\, artists\, and locals together for three unforgettable d
 ays of screenings\, conversations\, live events\, and connection. Hosted a
 t the historic Monte Rio Theater and neighboring venues in Monte Rio\, Cal
 ifornia\, River & Redwoods showcases narrative films\, documentaries\, sho
 rts\, student films\, and emerging voices from the Bay Area and beyond. Mo
 re than just a film festival\, River & Redwoods is about gathering in a be
 autiful small-town setting to experience great storytelling together. Expe
 ct filmmaker Q&As\, outdoor gatherings\, music\, local food and drink\, an
 d the laid-back creative spirit of Sonoma County. Whether you're an indust
 ry professional\, aspiring filmmaker\, or simply someone who loves movies 
 under the redwoods\, we invite you to spend the weekend with us.
LOCATION:D
URL:https://creativesonoma.org/event/river-redwoods-film-festival/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Taste of Italy at Centennial Mountain Tasting Room
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T170000
UID:260430TDPHz5wvYkaWPnNAHor2fw
DESCRIPTION:For wine drinkers eager to experience world-class wines made i
 n California from Italian varieties\, the Centennial Mountain Tasting Room
  is a must during any trip to Sonoma County. Located just off the plaza in
  the charming town of Healdsburg near famed restaurants\, boutiques and ga
 lleries\, the Centennial Mountain Tasting Room is a destination that invit
 es discovery. Founded by the acclaimed team that guides renowned Pinot Noi
 r and Chardonnay producer Rhys Vineyards\, Centennial Mountain was establi
 shed to explore Italian grape varieties grown on its acclaimed Centennial 
 Mountain Vineyard in the rugged mountains of Northern Sonoma County.\n\nTh
 e Centennial Mountain Vineyard Tasting features the winery’s coveted Neb
 biolo\, and the pioneering Carricante and Nerello Mascalese wines\, among 
 others. To showcase how beautifully the wines pair with food\, the winery 
 also offers a delicious Wine and Sushi Pairing from nearby Asahi Sushi\, o
 ne of Healdsburg’s most popular dining destinations.\n\nGuests can also 
 enhance their tasting experience with a curated salumi board from Journeym
 an Meat Company. This generous accompaniment features six house-made salum
 i\, crostini\, cornichons\, olives\, and a selection of local cheese that 
 serves 2 to 5 guests.
LOCATION:Centennial Mountain Tasting Room
URL:https://cmvineyard.com/visit/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Slave Play - a Left Edge Theatre Production
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T213000
UID:260924iZBvZ5qVIk-Isdow3SaoUg
DESCRIPTION:Presented by Left Edge Theatre. At the MacGregor Plantation\, 
 the antebellum South collides with the present in a provocative fever drea
 m where race\, desire\, gender\, and power intertwine. Nothing is quite as
  it seems—and yet everything is. Jeremy O. Harris’s explosive\, award-
 winning Slave Play rips apart the boundaries between history and modern Am
 erica\, confronting the enduring legacy of slavery and the complex interse
 ctions of race\, gender\, and sexuality. Recommended for ages 17\\+. Conta
 ins nudity\, sexual content\, simulated sexual violence\, and racially vio
 lent language. TICKETS ZONE A \\(Close to the action\\) $45 ZONE B \\(Midd
 le of the house\\) $35 ZONE C \\(In the back\\) $25 Tickets at Door - $45 
 - So buy in advance! SPECIAL DATES Thu 9/25: OPENING NIGHT & PARTY - Stick
  around to celebrate after the show! Wed 9/30: Industry Night - Calling al
 l theatre people! All tickets $20. Thur 10/1: Discount night - $10 off all
  tickets Advance purchase strongly encouraged.
LOCATION:The California
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/1504927394656747/1504928374656649/?act
 ive_tab=about
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
