BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Golden Hour
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260930T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260930T170000
UID:260903Fk5G4K8cNkqddsHoWXCcdA
DESCRIPTION:This September and October\, **Lucci Lambrusco is taking over
  Golden Hour at El Dorado Kitchen**\, bringing a taste of Italian aperi
 tivo culture to the patio all season long.\n\nSettle in for a late afterno
 on of Lucci Lambrusco\, Italian wines\, cocktails and shareable bites made
  for lingering. Throughout the two-month takeover\, Lucci will be joined e
 very Thursday by a rotating lineup of guest wineries\, importers and produ
 cers\, each stopping by to pour something special and share a little more 
 about what’s in your glass.\n\nThe season kicks off on **Thursday\, Sep
 tember 3**\, with live music\, Lucci Lambrusco\, passed pizzas and arancin
 i on the patio.\n\n**LUCCI ITALIAN GOLDEN HOUR TAKEOVER** Monday–Frid
 ay | 3:00–5:00 PM September & October\n\n**THURSDAY GUEST WINE SERIES** 
 Every Thursday | 3:00–5:00 PM\n\nSeptember 3 | Lucci Lambrusco\n\nSeptem
 ber 10 | Oliver McCrum Wines\n\nSeptember 17 | Mora Estate\n\nSeptember 24
  | Idlewild Wines\n\nOctober 1 | Cline Family Cellars\n\nOctober 8 | Unti 
 Vineyards\n\nOctober 15 | Massican\n\n...and more to come!\n\n**Lucci is p
 ouring all season long\, with a few friends joining along the way.**\n\nCo
 me for a glass. Stay for another.\n\n**JOIN US FOR GOLDEN HOUR**
LOCATION:El Dorado Hotel
URL:https://eldoradosonoma.com/el-dorado-kitchen/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Kendra Scott “Born to Shine” Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260930T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260930T203000
UID:260823Cwn2B9dcQkme4f4wbmKjXw
DESCRIPTION:Join us at the new Kendra Scott store in Montgomery Village fo
 r a two-part book club experience! Throughout the month\, we’ll read Ken
 dra Scott’s Born To Shine together while building community and creating
  deeper connection with women across Sonoma County.\n\nAttire: Come wearin
 g whatever makes you feel confident and comfortable. Stretchy pants & tenn
 is shoes are always acceptable at She Can Club!\n\nPart 1: Wednesday 8/26 
 6:30 – 8:30pm: Book Club Kickoff\n\nPick up your hardcover copy of Born 
 to Shine and meet your fellow book club members. We’ll spend the evening
  getting to know one another\, sharing what brought us to the book club\, 
 and launching our Instagram group chat so we can stay connected and encour
 age each other between events.\n\nPart 2: Wednesday 9/30\, 6:30–8:30pm: 
 Bedazzle & Reflect\n\nReunite with the group for a fun and creative book c
 over bedazzling party. As we craft\, we’ll explore the reflection questi
 ons from the back of the book\, voluntarily share our biggest takeaways\, 
 celebrate one another’s growth\, and deepen the connections we’ve buil
 t throughout the month.\n\nBoth events include:\n\n• A non-alcoholic Sip
  & Shop and Color Bar® experience\n\n• Light bites and non-alcoholic re
 freshments\n\n• Access to the Instagram group chat\n\n• All bedazzling
  supplies\n\n• A hardcover copy of Born to Shine ($28 value)\n\nAs an ad
 ded bonus\, Kendra Scott will donate 20% of event sales to She Can Club to
  further support women in Sonoma County.\n\nThe $40 ticket price includes 
 access to both events. Due to the nature of the experience and included ma
 terials\, tickets cannot be discounted for attendees who are only able to 
 attend one event.\n\nSorry\, no refunds as spots are limited at this event
 .\n\nIf you have any questions\, please email Hilary at heyhilary@shecancl
 ub.com or DM her on Instagram @shecanclub.
LOCATION:Kendra Scott in Montgomery Village
URL:https://montgomeryvillageca.com/event/kendra-scott-born-to-shine-book-
 club/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
