BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cuban Salsa Beginner - 4-Week Class
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261001T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261001T203000
UID:260914wLj0AVAZ0UiEm-UuAXdY1A
DESCRIPTION:Cuban Salsa Class with Eric Celestino & Abigail Celestino\n\n4
 week class\n\nOctober 1 – October 22\n\nClass requires a minimum of 8 re
 gistrations to run. Please register soon so we can secure the session!\n\n
 This is a beginner cuban salsa—you will learn your basic footwork and tu
 rns.\n\nIn this class\, you will learn the fundamentals of Cuban Salsa\, i
 ncluding body movement\, rhythm\, musicality\, footwork\, partner connecti
 on\, and partnerwork patterns inspired by authentic Cuban dance culture. W
 e focus on proper technique\, coordination\, flow\, and natural body expre
 ssion\, while also building confidence and strong foundations.\n\nClasses 
 are structured with:\n\n• Warm-up and body movement\n\n• Footwork and 
 rhythm exercises\n\n• Partnerwork technique\n\n• Short combinations an
 d practical applications\n\nOur goal is to help you understand how to danc
 e salsa\, not just memorize steps — developing timing\, connection\, and
  a comfortable\, joyful way of dancing.\n\nCome dance with us\, grow your 
 technique\, and experience the energy and flavor of Cuba in a supportive a
 nd welcoming environment.\n\nBook your spot\n\nDate & Time:\n\n4week class
 \, October 1 – October 22\n\nThursdays @ 7:30 PM\n\nAddress: 4140 Redwoo
 d Highway \\#8 San Rafael\, CA\n\nNote: Arrive 10 minutes before. No floor
  marking shoe soles allowed.
LOCATION:Salsa Dance Marin
URL:https://salsadancemarin.com/cuban-salsa/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Caring at the End of Life: Understanding Hospice & Palliative Care
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261001T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261001T193000
UID:260911cv5XD7SzXkylOD7jk2nfBg
DESCRIPTION:What does it really mean to care for someone facing serious il
 lness or nearing the end of life?\n\nJoin us for October’s Death Positiv
 e Event with local specialists **Cat and Lisa** for a thoughtful\, practic
 al conversation about the care and support available to individuals and fa
 milies navigating serious illness\, dying\, and end of life.\n\nWe’ll ex
 plore:\n\n🍃 The difference between hospice and palliative care 🍃 Whe
 n each type of care may be appropriate 🍃 What hospice care really looks
  like 🍃 How hospice supports both patients and families 🍃 The meanin
 gful role of hospice volunteers 🍃 How presence and companionship can ma
 ke a difference at the end of life\n\nWhether you’re caring for someone 
 now\, wondering what these services actually provide\, interested in volun
 teering\, or simply want to be better informed before the need arises\, th
 is evening offers an opportunity to learn\, ask questions\, and better und
 erstand the choices and support available.\n\n**Open to all & admission is
  FREE!**
LOCATION:Napa Valley Unitarian Universalists (NVUU) 
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/1999002056964
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
