BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Antarctica: The Frozen Desert | Photographs by Vegar Abelsnes
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261001T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261001T170000
UID:260914cqR5xRqhME-OvFb7oqiacw
DESCRIPTION:1st Street Gallery at WTRSHD will present *“Antarctica: The 
 Frozen Desert\,”* a new body of fine art photography by Vegar Abelsnes\,
  opening September 26th\, 2026\, and on view September through November. 
  The exhibition marks a deliberate turn in Abelsnes’ photography\; after
  more than two decades of working in a commercial and advertising capacity
 \, he has embarked on a career as a photo and field guide in the polar reg
 ions. The exhibit features work generated over 6 *voyages to the* Antarcti
 c Peninsula. He is returning to Antarctica in January and will add the Fal
 klands and South Georgia to his list of destinations to guide and photogra
 ph.\n\nTraveling to some of the most remote and inhospitable coastlines on
  Earth\, Abelsnes has photographed a landscape that exists almost entirely
  outside of human time. The ice in these images began forming millions of 
 years ago\, while Homo sapiens have only existed for roughly 300\,000 year
 s. Defined by such a scale\, Antarctica is less a place than a record — 
 vast\, indifferent\, treacherous\, and staggeringly beautiful\, holding a 
 kind of cosmic truth that Abelsnes says is more important now than ever be
 fore.
LOCATION:1st Street Gallery @ WTRSHD
URL:https://vegarabelsnes.com/ANTARCTICA:-The-Frozen-Desert/thumbs
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:California Native Creations Art Show
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261001T083000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261001T163000
UID:260909bIa9wUicJU-ekC2GzCdxLQ
DESCRIPTION:**September is the 17th Annual Pomo Honoring Month.** On Monda
 y\, Sept. 14\, the 6th California Native Creations Art Show opens Person S
 enior Wing\, Finley Community Center\, 2060 W. College Ave.\, Santa Rosa\,
  CA. The show is free and open to the public Monday – Friday\, 8:30 a.m.
 -4:30 p.m.\, through November 19.\n\nThe established and up-and-coming nat
 ive artists create with digital media\, paint and traditional materials in
  their art\, weaving\, regalia\, beadwork\, jewelry\, baskets and quilts.
  The artists include:\n\n·         Meyo Marrufo\, painter\, gues
 t curator for the de Young Museum and the Sonoma Valley Art Museum\,\n\n·
          Buffie Campbell\, Vice Chair\, Sherwood Valley Rancheria\
 , cultural teacher and master basket maker\,\n\n·         Henry E
 dward Frank\, *Yurok/Kashaya Pomo*\, who will show paintings and work with
  Legos titled *Mind Prison\,*\n\n·         Digital artist Nicolas
  (Nico) Vargas\, *Kashia Band of Pomo Indians*\, whose art was featured at
  the 55th Annual Stanford Powwow.\n\n·         plus Gloria Carret
 ero\; Rose Hammock\; Rudy Hammock\; Jocelyn Garcia\; Arella Ortega LaRose\
 , *Kashia Band of Pomo Indians*\; Angelica Smith\, *Manchester Point Arena
  and Yokayo Rancheria*\; Maria Pasalo\; Michelle Napoli\; Martina Morgan\,
  *Kashia Band of Pomo Indians*\; Hands Lopez\; Shashoni Hanover-Redenbaug
 h\; Katie Williams-Elliott\, Juan Partida\, and Mia Pasalo\, *Big Valley P
 omo Tribe*.
LOCATION:Person Senior Wing\, Finley Community Center
URL:http://www.pomoproject.org/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
