BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:An Evening with Wolf Run
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261002T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261002T223000
UID:2609161lZqa9hI5kaJH6dbI7Lh0g
DESCRIPTION:Wolf Run The beginnings of Wolf Run germinated in 2010 when A
 dam Traum and Jack Hines met at an open mic in Sonoma\, California. The tw
 o started chatting\, and got together shortly after that to jam on a rainy
  winter afternoon in a cabin in Glen Ellen. Traum got home and told his wi
 fe\, "I think I found my bassist!"\n\nAs they began playing local gigs\, a
 nd later traveling to out-of-town shows\, their bond grew and cemented the
 ir friendship. The duo needed a name and liked the idea of "Wolf Run\," a 
 neighborhood near Hines' house\, not far from Jack London State Park.\n\nT
 he mostly original music they play makes it difficult to put Wolf Run in a
  box. They fluidly move between songs in a wide range of genres that inclu
 de Americana\, blues\, folk\, country and rock while still sounding cohesi
 ve. Adam Traum is a prolific songwriter\, often enlisting the help of Hine
 s to bring a song home. Hines brings some terrific songs to the band as we
 ll.\n\nSubbing for veteran drummer Kendrick Freeman\, is another pro\, Gab
 e Ford\, who has toured with Little Feat and many other bands. The band pl
 ays songs ranging from acoustic singer-songwriter feels\, to funky grooves
 \, and full-tilt rock and roll.\n\nhttps://www.wolfrun.net\n\nhttps://www.
 facebook.com/WolfRun707/\n\nhttps://www.instagram.com/adam\\_traum/
LOCATION:The Lost Church Santa Rosa
URL:https://thelostchurch.my.salesforce-sites.com/ticket#/instances/a0FUh0
 00009FAZlMAO
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
