BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:California Native Creations Art Show
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261002T083000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261002T163000
UID:260909GgdA8yACSU-MutxhkHpYNQ
DESCRIPTION:**September is the 17th Annual Pomo Honoring Month.** On Monda
 y\, Sept. 14\, the 6th California Native Creations Art Show opens Person S
 enior Wing\, Finley Community Center\, 2060 W. College Ave.\, Santa Rosa\,
  CA. The show is free and open to the public Monday – Friday\, 8:30 a.m.
 -4:30 p.m.\, through November 19.\n\nThe established and up-and-coming nat
 ive artists create with digital media\, paint and traditional materials in
  their art\, weaving\, regalia\, beadwork\, jewelry\, baskets and quilts.
  The artists include:\n\n·         Meyo Marrufo\, painter\, gues
 t curator for the de Young Museum and the Sonoma Valley Art Museum\,\n\n·
          Buffie Campbell\, Vice Chair\, Sherwood Valley Rancheria\
 , cultural teacher and master basket maker\,\n\n·         Henry E
 dward Frank\, *Yurok/Kashaya Pomo*\, who will show paintings and work with
  Legos titled *Mind Prison\,*\n\n·         Digital artist Nicolas
  (Nico) Vargas\, *Kashia Band of Pomo Indians*\, whose art was featured at
  the 55th Annual Stanford Powwow.\n\n·         plus Gloria Carret
 ero\; Rose Hammock\; Rudy Hammock\; Jocelyn Garcia\; Arella Ortega LaRose\
 , *Kashia Band of Pomo Indians*\; Angelica Smith\, *Manchester Point Arena
  and Yokayo Rancheria*\; Maria Pasalo\; Michelle Napoli\; Martina Morgan\,
  *Kashia Band of Pomo Indians*\; Hands Lopez\; Shashoni Hanover-Redenbaug
 h\; Katie Williams-Elliott\, Juan Partida\, and Mia Pasalo\, *Big Valley P
 omo Tribe*.
LOCATION:Person Senior Wing\, Finley Community Center
URL:http://www.pomoproject.org/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Haunted Wine Tour & Tasting
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261002T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261002T173000
UID:2608314I9YLNQOnUyebmnrxsRvXQ
DESCRIPTION:This fall\, Buena Vista Winery invites you to uncover the myst
 eries\, legends\, and ghostly encounters woven into more than 165 years of
  history. Led by Sonoma historian and actor George Webber\, this immersive
  90 minute experience journeys through the historic Press House and Champa
 gne Cellars\, revealing true tales of unexplained happenings reported by B
 uena Vista team members and visitors throughout the years.\n\nHear the sto
 ries of the Glowing Ghostly Shirt\, the Little Girl Who Says Hi\, the myst
 erious Ghost Party on the Second Floor\, the Old Man Who Walked Into a Sto
 ne Wall\, and other strange occurrences that continue to add to the legend
  of Buena Vista.\n\nAlong the way\, explore some of the winery’s most in
 triguing spaces\, including the Bubble Lounge\, Cave of Curiosities\, and 
 Wine Tool Museum\, while enjoying five Buena Vista wines tasted throughout
  the experience\, including a taste drawn directly from barrel.\n\nAnd\, a
 s with any journey through Buena Vista’s extraordinary past\, you never 
 quite know when the winery’s legendary founder\, Count Agoston Haraszthy
 \, may choose to make an appearance.\n\nHistory\, wine\, mystery\, and per
 haps a spirit or two await.
LOCATION:Buena Vista Historical Winery
URL:https://eventvesta.com/events/160340/t/tickets
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
