BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Hallberg Butterfly Gardens Fall Plant Sale & Fundraiser
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T160000
UID:260922LDwo1fkCcE2xOBF27Iv8hQ
DESCRIPTION:Hallberg Butterfly Gardens’ **Fall Native Plant Sale & Fundr
 aiser** is coming up October 2nd & 3rd\, from 9:00 am–4:00 pm!\n\nOur nu
 rsery focuses on California native plants that support local wildlife and 
 pollinators—especially butterflies and moths. Whether you’re adding a 
 few natives to your garden\, creating a backyard wildlife habitat\, or loo
 king for host and nectar plants\, we’ll have a wide variety to choose fr
 om.\n\nFall is an excellent time to plant California native plants.  This
  year’s sale will include red-flowering currant\, seaside daisy\, Dougla
 s iris\, Dutchman’s pipevine\, western azalea\, blue elderberry\, tiger 
 lily\, hedgerow plants\, and much more.\n\nPlant lists organized by bloom 
 time and butterfly and moth host plants will be available at the sale\, an
 d our knowledgeable staff will be on hand to help answer questions and hel
 p you choose plants for your garden.\n\nBecause parking at Hallberg Butter
 fly Gardens is limited\, the plant sale is by appointment.\n\nReserve a ti
 me and view the complete plant list on our website: https://hallbergbutter
 flygardens.org/our-nursery\n\nAfter your nursery appointment\, you’re we
 lcome to stay and enjoy a self-guided walk through the Gardens.\n\nYour pl
 ant purchases support Hallberg Butterfly Gardens and our work creating and
  caring for habitat for butterflies\, moths\, pollinators\, and other loca
 l wildlife.\n\nWe hope to see you at the Gardens!
LOCATION:Hallberg Butterfly Gardens
URL:https://hallbergbutterflygardens.org/our-nursery
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:1TRIBE: Reggae • Dancehall • Afrobeats • Amapiano with Konne
 x & Kobie
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T210000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261004T013000
UID:2609220UF0AVXREUGIx-n85hXEOQ
DESCRIPTION:1TRIBE: Reggae • Dancehall • Afrobeats • Amapiano with K
 onnex & Kobie\n\n1TRIBE returns to Barrel Proof Lounge for another night o
 f Reggae\, Dancehall\, Afrobeats & Amapiano in Downtown Santa Rosa.\n\nKon
 nex Productions and Barrel Proof Lounge bring 1TRIBE back on Saturday\, Oc
 tober 3\, turning the lounge into a late-night dance floor powered by soun
 ds from Africa\, the Caribbean and across the global club scene.\n\nBehind
  the decks are DJ Konnex & DJ Kobie\, two selectors with deep roots in the
  music and a serious range between them.\n\nDJ KONNEX Voted 2025 NorBay Be
 st Live DJ\, Santa Rosa's Konnex has built a reputation for sets that move
  fluidly across reggae\, dancehall\, Afrobeats and global club sounds. Rat
 her than simply jumping from track to track\, his sets are built as a jour
 ney — digging deep\, changing gears and keeping the dance floor moving.\
 n\nDJ KOBIE Born in Trinidad & Tobago and now based in the Bay Area\, Kobi
 e Quashie brings an international sound-system pedigree to 1TRIBE. He foun
 ded Ashanti Hi Fi SoundSystem and has performed across California and arou
 nd the world\, including Trinidad\, Jamaica\, Brazil\, Mexico\, South Afri
 ca and Ethiopia. His musical range reaches through reggae\, dancehall\, Af
 robeat\, Afro House\, Soca\, hip-hop and electronic music\, while keeping 
 Caribbean sound-system culture at the heart of the mix.\n\nTogether\, Konn
 ex and Kobie created 1TRIBE around a simple idea: African rhythm\, Caribbe
 an energy and global dance music sharing the same room. Afrobeats rolls in
 to Amapiano. Reggae gives way to Dancehall. The tempo changes\, the bass s
 tays heavy\, and the dance floor connects it all.\n\nIf you caught 1TRIBE 
 at Barrel Proof in June\, you already know the energy. Now the tribe gathe
 rs again.\n\n1TRIBE  Reggae • Dancehall • Afrobeats • Amapiano\n\nL
 IMITED RESERVED TABLES\n\nWant a home base for the night? We have just 12 
 reserved tables available for $69 each.\n\nEach table includes:\n\nReserve
 d seating for 4 Your own call button for beverage service A guaranteed spo
 t to sit down between trips to the dance floor\n\nOnly 12 tables are avail
 able\, so grab yours in advance if you want one.\n\n Saturday\, October 3
 \, 2026  9 PM  Barrel Proof Lounge — Downtown Santa Rosa  Konnex & Ko
 bie  $10 Presale  21+\n\nCome early. Stay late. Find your rhythm.\n\nBar
 rel Proof Lounge 501 Mendocino Ave Downtown Santa Rosa\n\nCheck out **www.
 BarrelProofLounge.com** for all sorts of good times ahead!
LOCATION:Barrel Proof Lounge
URL:https://1TribeOctober.eventbrite.com
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Adrian West Band
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T160000
UID:2609219ZyuQuK-vkmxXgdxE6ws2w
DESCRIPTION:Come hear the five-piece Adrian West Band perform in the beerg
 arden at Waterhawk Lake Club in Rohnert Park! Free show\, all ages \\(tips
  appreciated\\). We play from 4 - 7pm.\n\nAdrian West Band is a five-piece
  acoustic rock ensemble from Oakland. They play a fun mix of originals\, c
 overs and instrumentals plus a bit of jazz. Some have described their soun
 d as “Paul Simon meets Talking Heads”.\n\nAdrian enjoys setting philos
 ophical lyrics to joyful music. His topics may veer a tad dark at times bu
 t the underlying music is uplifting\, giving the listener a richly layered
  experience. Whether he's telling a story about a skinny-dipping episode g
 one awry or grappling with some major challenge facing humanity\, his lyri
 cs are infused with equal parts hope\, realism and whimsy.\n\nAdrian West 
 - vocals\, acoustic guitar\, elec. violin & live looping Larisa Roberts - 
 vocals\, percussion Chris Haag - alto sax JJ Hartmann - upright bass Nick 
 Sager - drums\n\nBand website: www.adrianwest.com\n\n------\n\nBrewsters B
 eer Garden is located in the historic district of downtown Petaluma. We ar
 e an open-air dining restaurant with over 350 seats.\n\nOur cuisine is foc
 used on technique driven dishes influenced by Southern Carolina BBQ and a 
 smattering of locally sourced and sustainably raised Petaluma producers an
 d ranchers. Think southern BBQ meets California produce with a refined tou
 ch of explosive flavors.\n\nThe dining space compliments the food perfectl
 y as guests are treated to outdoor seating in a historic setting\, with th
 e comforts of large heat lamps\, fire pit and live music stage.\n\nWe offe
 r an array of over 30 revolving local craft beers on draft\, Sonoma and Na
 pa Valley wine\, and a full selection of spirits and cocktails.\n\nBrewste
 rs was built for people that want more than just a good meal when they eat
 \, they want a dining experience. We are laid back\, kid & dog friendly\, 
 and like to have fun.\n\nMore at www.brewstersbeergarden.com
LOCATION:Waterhawk Lake Club
URL:https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/adrian-west-band/199643
 52/2026-10-03T16
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:SHANA MORRISON & Caledonia
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T220000
UID:260920vrkSAWBIIUiKarCSEkkzcA
DESCRIPTION:SHANA MORRISON's musical style has been called pop with a side
  of blues and a side of rock\, but she has never shied away from including
  other ingredients\, like country\, R&B\, and jazz into the mix. Her mater
 ial is ever-changing\, but what always remains the same is Shana’s uniqu
 e and wide-ranging voice. Her dynamic and charismatic talent has earned th
 e attention of national newspapers and magazines as well as airplay on maj
 or radio stations.The daughter of legendary Northern Irish musician Van Mo
 rrison\, Shana began performing with her group Caledonia in the San Franci
 sco Bay area in 1996\, releasing their debut CD on her own label\, Belfast
  Violet Records. Since 2002\, Shana has toured internationally\, including
  numerous concert dates with her father. Besides "Van the Man" she has sha
 red billing with the likes of Bonnie Raitt\, Peter Frampton\, John Lee Hoo
 ker\, and Dr. John\, and has played for a variety of festival audiences\, 
 including the San Francisco Blues Festival and the Cork Jazz Festival.  H
 er set list always includes some of Van Morrison’s greatest hits.
LOCATION:Rancho Nicasio
URL:https://www.friendsproductions.net/shows
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:GPGS: Sonoma by Design
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T173000
UID:2609196sLhzHSDOUaWQQr4HeOuag
DESCRIPTION:Hosted by Kathy O’Connor and Matt Larrabee Step inside one o
 f Sonoma’s most spectacular private residences for a rare and intimate e
 vening celebrating exceptional architecture\, inspired design\, and outsta
 nding food. Limited to just 25 guests\, this exclusive gathering offers an
  opportunity to explore a remarkable Sonoma home over cocktails before sit
 ting down to a very special dinner by Valley\, Sonoma’s Michelin Bib Gou
 rmand restaurant celebrated for vibrant\, seasonal Northern California coo
 king. Designed by architect Jeff Zimmerman of Zimmerman\\+Associates\, wit
 h interiors by acclaimed designer Becky Carter\, the home is a striking co
 ntemporary retreat where sophisticated city style meets the natural beauty
  of the Sonoma landscape. Soaring spaces\, dramatic sight lines\, custom d
 etails\, and seamless indoor-outdoor living create a residence that is as 
 compelling to experience as it is to admire. Join us for this rare opportu
 nity to take in the architecture and interiors up close and enjoy an excep
 tional culinary experience. Saturday\, October 3 | Cocktails & Dinner $400
  per person | Limited to 25 guests
LOCATION:Sonoma Valley Museum of Art
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/1593474102224515/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
