DESCRIPTION:Join us for an lively\, in-person marketplace bursting with un
 ique finds from over 125 talented artists\, crafters\, and vendors\, showc
 asing a exciting mix of creative treasures — from festive holiday décor
  and gifts to rare collectibles and one-of-a-kind art. Every day brings so
 mething new to explore!\n\nBrowse an incredible selection of products\, in
 cluding jewelry\, clothing\, art\, woodworking\, glasswork\, pottery\, kid
 s’ toys\, miniatures\, candles\, soaps\, and much more. Discover beautif
 ul vintage and handmade pieces\, plus practical essentials like pet access
 ories and gift cards.  Featuring tasty treats from Sax's Joint\, Sabor\, 
 Pupusas la Bendicion\, The Chicks with the Lemonade\, and more. Santa will
  visit to get an early look at those Wish Lists!\n\nProceeds from this eve
 nt benefit Micah’s Hugs\, an inspiring local nonprofit dedicated to educ
 ating youth about the dangers of substance abuse and fentanyl poisoning.\n
 \nOur 2025 Grand Bazaar welcomed more than 3\,000 community members and ra
 ised over $20\,000 to support this life-saving mission. Join us this year 
 for an even bigger\, better\, and more spacious event. Together\, we can m
 ake a meaningful difference for our youth—and you may even learn how to 
 save a life.
LOCATION:Petaluma Fairgrounds
URL:https://giving4life.org/2026-grand-bazaar/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Dear Evan Hansen
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261004T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261004T163000
UID:260911OhLwu0YcCkSoa4C9uQrZKQ
DESCRIPTION:Poignant\, raw\, and of-the-moment\, Dear Evan Hansen pulls ba
 ck the curtain on the profound desire for human connection in the digital 
 age\, offering an empathetic look at the alienation of young people naviga
 ting modern social pressures.\n\nThe story follows Evan\, a high school se
 nior struggling with severe social anxiety who writes motivational letters
  to himself as a therapeutic exercise. When a troubled classmate dies by s
 uicide with one of Evan’s letters in his pocket\, the boy's grieving par
 ents mistakenly believe Evan was his secret best friend. Desperate to comf
 ort them\, Evan plays along\, spiraling into a web of fabricated emails an
 d internet fame before he must ultimately face the truth.\n\nPowered by a 
 critically acclaimed pop-rock score and the sweeping anthems\, Dear Even H
 ansen is a powerful reminder that we are never truly alone. Spreckels is p
 roud to present the North Bay premiere of this six-time Tony Award winning
  musical!
LOCATION:Spreckels Center for the Performing Arts
URL:https://spreckelsonline.com/show/2026-27-season/dear-evan-hansen/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
