BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:THREE YEARS ON: PALESTINIAN GENOCIDE AND SHARED STRUGGLE
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261008T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261008T200000
UID:2609209K4Rwx8Waka6POIqc-c4Rg
DESCRIPTION:Palestinian American Tarik Kanaana and Jewish American Carol B
 loom\, both Sonoma County activists\, will share reflections and discuss a
 spects of the 3-year-long ongoing genocide of the Palestinian people.\n\nT
 hey will share personal experiences\, information\, perspectives\, quotes\
 , and poems on a variety of topics\, including:\n\n·       What is 
 it like to be a Palestinian citizen of Israel – a second-class citizen\n
 \n·       The interconnectedness between colonialism\, imperialism\
 , and racism\n\n·       Moving from ignorance/bias to anti-Zionism\
 n\n·       U.S. complicity with Israel and the work of Taxpayers Ag
 ainst Genocide\n\nThere will be ample time for Q&A and discussion among us
 . Invite your friends to join our dialogue. Open to everyone!\n\nEmail rac
 ialjusticeallies@gmail.com to register and we will send you a Zoom link on
  the day of the dialogue.
LOCATION:Zoom
URL:http://www.racialjusticeallies.org/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jack London’s Neighbors: The History of the Sonoma Developmental
  Center
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261008T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261008T113000
UID:260918yz82Pg4Np02xoPHXJqjj8Q
DESCRIPTION:Join historical ecologist Angela Nardo-Morgan for a look at th
 e early history of what became the Sonoma Developmental Center\, from its 
 origins in the late 19th century to its closure.\n\nPresented in partnersh
 ip with the Glen Ellen Historical Society\, the program will explore the f
 ounding of the institution at Eldridge in 1891\, its development and chang
 ing philosophies of care\, and the important role it played in shaping the
  surrounding Glen Ellen community. The program will also consider the broa
 der history of the area during the lifetimes of Jack and Charmian London\,
  including the institution’s proximity to London’s Beauty Ranch.\n\nNo
 te: This program focuses on the historical period of the Sonoma Developmen
 t Center up until its closure and does not cover current redevelopment pla
 ns or discussions.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/events/jl-sdc/ 
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Madrona Debuts Garden Supper Club in Healdsburg
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261008T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261008T193000
UID:260915jzt2bxyZwkyYT6bRHf8ynw
DESCRIPTION:On Thursday\, October 8 at 6pm\, The Madrona\, the two-MICHELI
 N Key boutique hotel and restaurant in Healdsburg\, will debut the inaugur
 al Madrona Garden Supper Club\, a new dining series celebrating the beauty
 \, abundance and changing seasons of the historic estate’s garden.\n\nDe
 signed as an intimate dinner party of just 30 guests\, The Madrona Garden 
 Supper Club offers a firsthand look at the property’s onsite regenerativ
 e gardens and how they drive the culinary program and seasonal menus. The 
 experience begins in the Citrus Grove with welcome cocktails (or spirit-fr
 ee alternatives) and seasonal canapés\, followed by a chef-guided walk th
 rough The Madrona’s garden to explore the harvested ingredients inspirin
 g the night’s menu. Guests will then sit down along Garden Lane for a fo
 ur-course dinner (and optional wine pairing) inspired entirely by what is 
 growing in the garden at that very moment.\n\n**What:** The Madrona Garden
  Supper Club: Autumn\n\n**When:** Thursday\, October 8 at 6pm\n\n**Where:*
 * The Madrona\, 1001 Westside Road\, Healdsburg\n\n**Price:** $150 per per
 son with optional wine or non-alcoholic pairing ($65 per person)\n\n**RSVP
 :** Seats are limited\, so RSVPs through OpenTable are required.\n\nThe Ma
 drona Garden Supper Club will continue to evolve with the seasons\, with n
 ew dates in 2027 to be announced and each menu curated around what’s fre
 shest in the garden.
LOCATION:The Madrona
URL:https://www.opentable.com/booking/experiences-availability?rid=8088&re
 stref=8088&experienceId=791873&utm_source=external&utm_medium=referral&utm
 _campaign=shared
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
