DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261008T235900
UID:260924XAg47ErcZkOmsNO5bwrXKA
DESCRIPTION:THURSDAY NIGHTS WITH DJ BRXNDO OPEN FORMAT • REQUESTS • DA
 NCING • NO COVER\n\nThursday nights have a new home in The Lounge at Bar
 rel Proof. Every Thursday at 9 PM\, DJ BRXNDO takes over the front room wi
 th an open-format set built around the crowd\, the dance floor and your re
 quests.\n\nBRXNDO has been making his way through the Bay Area nightlife s
 cene\, spinning parties from Santa Rosa to San Francisco. Now he's settlin
 g into a weekly Thursday night residency at Barrel Proof.\n\nOpen format m
 eans just that: no single genre gets to run the night. BRXNDO can move thr
 ough Reggaeton\, Hip-Hop\, Latin hits\, Top 40\, throwbacks\, dance tracks
  and party favorites depending on where the room takes him.\n\nHear someth
 ing you want? Make a request.\n\nSome Thursdays might lean Latin. Some mig
 ht turn into a throwback party. Some nights might go somewhere completely 
 different. BRXNDO reads the room and keeps it moving.\n\nWhatever else is 
 happening at Barrel Proof that night\, The Lounge belongs to BRXNDO every 
 Thursday at 9.\n\nDJ BRXNDO Every Thursday 9 PM The Lounge at Barrel Proof
  501 Mendocino Ave • Downtown Santa Rosa 21+ No Cover\n\nCheck out **www
 .BarrelProofLounge.com** for all sorts of good times ahead!
LOCATION:Barrel Proof Lounge
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/thursday-nights-with-dj-brxndo-live-in-th
 e-lounge-tickets-2002239002756?aff=oddtdtcreator
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Marin Farmers Markets
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261008T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261008T130000
UID:260924NgJBCN1SnEyeRwuv9Si5zg
DESCRIPTION:Price: Free\n\nSponsor: Marin Center\n\nExplore the bounty of 
 summer at the Marin Farmers Markets. Taste vine-ripened tomatoes\, corn th
 at was picked that morning\, and peaches so juicy you have to bend over ju
 st to get a bite. Farm-fresh eggs\, grass-fed beef\, artisan c heeses\, ra
 w milk\, and freshly baked breads complete the shopping exper ience. Speci
 alty prepared foods and handmade art add to the magic of the market.\n\nEn
 joy the intimate feeling of the Thursday Marin Farmers Market\, an ideal p
 lace to meet for lunch and pick up fresh produce for the weekend. Discover
  the abundance and diversity of product at the celebrated Sunday Marin Far
 mers Market\, the third largest farmers market in California. Turn your do
 llar into a vote for local sustainable agriculture\, shrink your eco-footp
 rint\, and revive the feeling of being intimate ly connected to your food 
 by meeting your farmers face-to-face. The market takes place rain or shine
 .\n\nwww.aginstitutemarin.org
LOCATION:Marin Veterans' Memorial Auditorium
URL:https://www.marincounty.gov/county-marin-calendar
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Dia de Muertos at Jack London State Historic Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261008T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261008T170000
UID:260921t4kQx6WUHE63F_k6EuywEg
DESCRIPTION:In recognition of Día de Muertos\, Jack London State Historic
  Park will present two *ofrendas* in the House of Happy Walls Museum from 
 Oct. 4 to Nov. 6\, 2026.\n\nDia de Muertos\, or Day of the Dead\, is a tra
 dition that began in Mexican and other Latino cultures.  An ofrenda\, Spa
 nish for ‘offering\,’ is an altar created to honor and welcome the mem
 ory of those who have died.\n\nThe Legacy Ofrenda will honor writer and ad
 venturer Jack London\, Charmian London\, and other individuals connected t
 o the history of the property. Through photographs\, reproductions\, tradi
 tional elements of an ofrenda\, and carefully selected symbolic objects\, 
 the installation will reflect Jack and Charmian's partnership\, writing an
 d travels\, their life at Beauty Ranch\, their connection to the land\, an
 d the legacies they left behind.\n\nThe Community Ofrenda will be a shared
 \, participatory offering. Visitors\, locals\, volunteers\, Board members\
 , and employees can contribute a small photograph\, written name\, memory\
 , drawing or message honoring someone who has passed away – including a 
 beloved pet. \n\nThe installation will grow throughout October as more pe
 ople participate.  Materials will be available at the display for visitor
 s who would like to join the celebration and contribute a name\, memory or
  even a drawing of their loved one.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/dia-de-muertos-2026/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Gallery Route One Events
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261008T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261008T170000
UID:260921D3QdUCJ5F0u1jHDDNXLajQ
DESCRIPTION:On Saturday October 3\, Gallery Route One in Point Reyes Sta
 tion opens three news exhibitions: Bruce Mitchell’s Gravitational Pull
 \, fine-art wood sculpture\; Steven Hurwitz’s abstract multimedia wall c
 onstructions\; and Geoffrey Campen’s Offcut\, mixed-media work based on
  architectural plans\; The public is cordially invited to the opening\, O
 ctober 3\, 3 to 5pm. Meet GRO Artists\, see the show\, and enjoy a glass 
 of wine. Shows run until November 8\, open 11am to 5pm\, Thurs through Mon
 . https://galleryrouteone.org
LOCATION:Gallery Route One
URL:https://galleryrouteone.org
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Exhibit: Aspirations
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261008T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261008T180000
UID:260916wfImFmv06UaBdv7PihdyEw
DESCRIPTION:Date: FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE  9/15/26\n\nOCTOBER EXHIBIT: ASPI
 RATIONS\n\nEXHIBIT DATES – September 28 – October 25\, 2026\n\nRECEPTI
 ON: SATURDAY\, October 3\, 2026\, 3-6 pm: Join us to meet Laura Roney and 
 Linda Loveland Reid and learn about their art and inspiration.  Be sure t
 o take part in the Gallery’s free monthlong drawing for a beautiful work
  by a Gallery artist.  Refreshments will be served.\n\nSonoma County arti
 st\, Laura Roney\, unveils Aspirations\, a new collection of paintings in 
 oil\, celebrating the unique differing goals people set during our lives\,
  challenging us to take bold steps forward.  Of universal inspiration\, A
 spiration and Awe splashes the Milky Way’s starry brilliance across the 
 heavens\, capturing our imagination and hope as worldly cares are left beh
 ind.  Moving from natural forces to human endeavor\, looking toward socia
 l change\, Aspiring to Vote\, the portrait of a hopeful suffragette\, evok
 es the dream for a better future.  A lifetime goal for many\, the maratho
 n\, Aspiring for 26.2\, captures the early morning excitement waiting for 
 start times.  “People doing ordinary things but dreaming larger for the
  future has been a great inspiration for this series.  I hope folks will 
 be inspired by the boldness of people’s dreams\,” commented Roney on h
 er inspiration for the work.\n\nArt has been a lifelong passion for Roney.
   Beginning her art studies at a young age\, whatever avenue she was purs
 uing in life\, she continued her artistic endeavors.  After a successful 
 career in microbiology and pharmaceutical research\, a family move to Nort
 hern California enabled Roney to focus on her art.  She received her MFA 
 from Academy of Art University\, San Francisco.\n\nMeet the artist: Roney 
 will host the Gallery on September 30 and October 1 from 11am to 6 pm.\n\n
 The Stairway Smallworks Showcase features Linda Loveland Reid’s Intentio
 nal Chaos\, a collection of exciting mixed-media works that explode with e
 xcitement and energy. Random patterns\, amorphous shapes and dancing dribb
 les magically coalesce into bold statements.  Intriguing and compelling\,
  like interlocking gears\, in Patterns of Memory multiple patterns interlo
 ck on fields of gold and black.  “I love throwing ink\, paint and even 
 coffee onto a blank canvas and creating through instinct\, gesture and emo
 tion.  Distilling energy into smaller works brings new challenges and som
 e happy surprises\,” noted Reid on her creative process.\n\nMeet the art
 ist: Reid will host the Gallery on October 23 from 11am to 6 pm.\n\n Also
  join us for ART NITE HEALDSBURG\, Thursday\, October 1\, 5 – 7 pm.  AR
 T NITE Healdsburg\, held the 1st Thursday of Every Month\, is a community 
 event celebrating art and creativity with over 20 galleries participating.
   ArtNiteHealdsburg.com.\n\nUpstairs Art Gallery\, 306 Center Street\, He
 aldsburg\, CA 95448. \\(707\\) 431-4214.: OPEN DAILY: 11am – 6 pm.   
  www.upstairsart gallery.net \n\nFor further information: Contact: Beverly
  Bird\, Press Contact\, at bvdrio@sonic.net or 707-799-1490.
LOCATION:Upstairs Art Gallery
URL:http://www.upstairsartgallery.net
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
