SUMMARY:Decorative Fruit Tart Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261009T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261009T200000
UID:2609261FK-Iy6zKkafPt1MIgesRg
DESCRIPTION:Friday\, October 9\, 2026 5:30 pm to 8:00 pm\n\nLocation\n\nRo
 om 109\, Rotary Kitchen\n\nCategory\n\nCulinary Arts\n\nExperience Level\n
 \nBeginning\n\nAges\n\n18 and older\n\nRegistration Cost:\n\n$100\n\nMater
 ials:\n\nProvided\n\nTotal Registration Cost:\n\n$100\n\nHave you ever loo
 ked into a pastry case to see beautifully adorned fresh fruit tarts and wo
 ndered how they are made? Well\, look no further! In this class I will wal
 k you through all the steps to make stunning fruit tarts.Leaning into earl
 y Fall season we will be making poached pear and pear butter tartlets usin
 g intensely floral pears from Little Saint Farm\, beautifully sweet fresh 
 figs paired with a fig leave pastry cream\, and a nice bright zingy citrus
  curd to round it all out and give you a good range of skills to work with
 .We will be working with Pate Sucree\, a sweet and delicate pastry dough t
 hat has many applications. To add depth of flavor and wholesome nutrition 
 I will be adding locally grown and milled whole grain flour from Farmer Ma
 i in Sebastopol.Food and Beverages will be provided and after class you wi
 ll take home the mini tartlets decorated in class\, as well as a full 8”
  tart shell and local Little Saint Pears to get you started at home!With a
 ll of the skills you learn in this class you can really mix and match reci
 pes to build your own creations! Come to connect\, make edible art\, and h
 ave a good time!
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/decorative-fruit-tart-works
 hop/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
