DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T200000
UID:260924B9RuFx9q0kmOthFqJxB42Q
DESCRIPTION:Polenta & Stew Dinner – Oct. 10\, 2026 - benefit dinner\n\n
  WHERE:           Penngrove Community Clubhouse\, 385 Woodward
  Avenue\, Penngrove\n\n WHEN:            Saturday\, October 1
 0\, 2026 – Social Hour 5:30 pm\,  Dinner 6:30 pm\n\n TICKETS:    
       $30.00\; children 12 and under $15  - Tickets are by cash or
  check at Soap Cauldron (red barn at the end of Penngrove Station)\, 1183
 0 Main St.\, Penngrove.  \n\nOr online at: https://polenta\\_penngrove.e
 ventbrite.com \n\n WHY:               A benefit for Penng
 rove Park and Clubhouse improvements and the support of our community.\n\n
  CONTACT FOR MORE INFO: Kim Hanson\, (707) 318- 2191. Or go to https://w
 ww.penngrovesocialfiremen.org\n\n **POLENTA AND STEW DINNER BENEFITS PENN
 GROVE PARK AND CLUBHOUSE – Oct. 10\, 2026**\n\n Join us for a cozy even
 ing of hearty polenta and stew\, all for a good cause on\n\nSaturday\, Oct
 ober 10\, 2026\, at Penngrove Community Clubhouse\, 385 Woodward Avenue\,
  Penngrove.  \n\n This is a meal that old-time farmers ate\, long befo
 re the term 'farm-to-table' was coined. Polenta and stew will be served wi
 th green salad\, French bread\, and dessert.  \n\n Social hour is at 5:
 30 pm\, with dinner at 6:30 pm. \n\n All proceeds benefit Penngrove Park
  and Clubhouse improvements. The nonprofit Penngrove Social Firemen sponso
 r the event. \n\n Tickets are $30\; children 12 and under are $15.  Bu
 y tickets with cash or check at Soap Cauldron\, 11830 Main St.\, or online
  at  https://polenta\\_penngrove.eventbrite.com\n\n For info\, call Kim
  Hanson at 707 318-2191 or see https://www.penngrovesocialfiremen.org\n\n
  See more at https://www.PenngroveSocialFiremen.org\n\nhttps://www.instag
 ram.com/penngrovesocialfiremen/\n\nhttps://www.facebook.com/groups/3393479
 40599\n\nhttps://www.visitpenngrove.com\n\n **About Penngrove Social Fire
 men**\n\nPenngrove Social Firemen was formed in 1946 to support the commun
 ity. The non-profit group owns and maintains Penngrove Park and Penngrove 
 Community Club for the enjoyment of all. Members need not reside in Penngr
 ove.
LOCATION:Penngrove Clubhouse
URL:https://www.penngrovesocialfiremen.org
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
