BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Headline Comedy - Joey Bragg – Live in Downtown Santa Rosa
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T210000
UID:260922UeAL3HHBDUixZZd2jxHH9Q
DESCRIPTION:Joey Bragg brings his stand-up to Barrel Proof Lounge for a sp
 ecial Saturday night comedy show in Downtown Santa Rosa!\n\nYou may know J
 oey Bragg as Joey Rooney from Disney Channel's hit series Liv and Maddie\,
  but long before television came calling\, Joey was already doing stand-up
  comedy.\n\nA Bay Area native\, Joey started writing jokes at just 12 year
 s old and began performing stand-up as a teenager before making the jump t
 o television and film. Along the way\, he's shared the stage with comedian
 s including Dane Cook\, Tim Allen and Bob Saget.\n\nHis breakout role came
  as Joey Rooney on Disney Channel's Liv and Maddie\, followed by an expand
 ing list of comedy credits on screens big and small. Joey starred opposite
  Kyra Sedgwick as Freddie Raines on ABC's Call Your Mother and opposite Da
 vid Spade and Nat Faxon in the Netflix/Happy Madison comedy Father of the 
 Year. He also appeared in Netflix's Wet Hot American Summer: Ten Years Lat
 er and starred in the indie comedy Sid Is Dead.\n\nAnd stand-up has remain
 ed part of the equation. In 2026\, Joey appeared at Netflix Is a Joke Fest
  in Los Angeles with Bragging Rights with Joey Bragg\, and he's back on th
 e road performing comedy around the country.\n\nNow he's coming home to No
 rthern California for a night of stand-up at Barrel Proof Lounge.\n\nVIP T
 ABLES\n\nMake a night of it with one of our $95 VIP tables for four.\n\nEa
 ch VIP table includes reserved seating for four\, your own call button for
  beverage service\, and your first round of beer/cider or a bottle of wine
 .\n\nEVENT DETAILS\n\n Saturday\, October 10\, 2026  7 PM  Barrel Proof
  Lounge — Downtown Santa Rosa  Joey Bragg  $15 Advance / $20 Door  VI
 P Table for 4 — $95  21+  2-drink minimum\n\nBarrel Proof Lounge 501 M
 endocino Ave Downtown Santa Rosa\n\nCheck out **www.BarrelProofLounge.com*
 * for all sorts of good times ahead!
LOCATION:Barrel Proof Lounge
URL:https://JoeyBragg.eventbrite.com
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Turn of the Century – High Energy Party Rock in Downtown Santa R
 osa
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T210000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261011T000000
UID:260922RovL-Iy5HUiP7DsWVET1UA
DESCRIPTION:Turn of the Century is back at Barrel Proof — with a new voi
 ce up front and a whole lot of songs you already know by heart.\n\nIf your
  ideal rock show jumps from Green Day to Sublime\, Foo Fighters to Beastie
  Boys\, Nirvana to No Doubt and Weezer to Alice in Chains\, you've found y
 our Saturday night.\n\nNorthern California's Turn of the Century describes
  itself as a “jukebox of high energy party rock hits\,” and that's a p
 retty accurate description. This isn't a band that stays politely inside o
 ne decade or one corner of rock & roll. Their setlist barrels through the 
 late ’80s\, ’90s and 2000s into the 2010s\, built around big riffs\, b
 ig choruses and songs that tend to turn an audience into backup singers.\n
 \nAnd this time\, there's a new singer behind the mic.\n\nTurn of the Cent
 ury has been leveling up its live show throughout 2026\, playing everywher
 e from clubs and breweries to the Lake County Fair and Santa Rosa's massiv
 e 90's Fest. Now they're bringing the party back to the Barrel Proof stage
  for a full Saturday night show.\n\nWHAT'S IN THE JUKEBOX?\n\nHow about 
 “Everlong\,” “Basket Case\,” “Santeria\,” “Smells Like Teen 
 Spirit\,” “Just a Girl\,” “Fight for Your Right\,” “Say It Ain
 't So\,” “The Middle\,” “My Own Worst Enemy\,” “Are You Gonna 
 Be My Girl\,” “Sweet Child O' Mine\,” “Creep\,” “Give It Away\
 ,” “The Kids Aren't Alright” and a whole lot more?\n\nYeah. That kin
 d of night.\n\nCome ready to sing. Come ready to dance. Come ready to sudd
 enly realize you apparently still know every word to a song you haven't th
 ought about since 2003.\n\nEVENT DETAILS\n\n Saturday\, October 10\, 2026
   9 PM  Barrel Proof Lounge — Downtown Santa Rosa  Turn of the Centur
 y  $5 Advance / $10 Door  21+\n\nGrab the cheap tickets in advance and s
 ave five bucks for something cold at the bar.\n\nBarrel Proof Lounge 501 M
 endocino Ave Downtown Santa Rosa\n\nCheck out **www.BarrelProofLounge.com*
 * for all sorts of good times ahead!
LOCATION:Barrel Proof Lounge
URL:https://TOTCBPL.eventbrite.com
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Novato Repair Fair & Halloween Swap
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T130000
UID:260921RSX7qJc6pk6IeKtXWzSotg
DESCRIPTION:Do you have a lamp\, small appliance\, textile\, or bike in ne
 ed of repair?\n\nBring it to the Repair Fair!‍ ‍\n\nVolunteers and spe
 cialized repair professionals will be on-hand to repair\\* your items.  
 We ask that you stay with your item while it's being fixed\, so you can le
 arn tips for future maintenance\, how to shop for repairable goods\, and e
 ven how to repair things yourself!  \n\nIf you’d like to bring an it
 em to repair\, please register the item here: https://www.reusealliance.or
 g/rf-reg\n\n\\(Pre-registering allows us to prepare for your item!\\)\n\nT
 his event will also feature a Halloween Costume & Decor Swap! Spooky Seaso
 n is around the corner - bring in your used costumes\, props\, and decor \
 \(must be clean and in good condition\\)\, and take home items that are ne
 w-to-you!\n\nThis is a free public event.\n\n\\*We cannot guarantee your i
 tem\\(s\\) will be repaired\, depending on the existing damage or breakage
 \, ability of volunteer fixers\, and availability of materials for repair.
  Note: we cannot work on microwaves\, repair screens on cell phones/comput
 er devices\, or perform any welding/brazing\, but we are happy to refer y
 ou to professionals who can. In addition\, the textile department is not a
 ble to perform the following:\n\nReplacing zippers\n\nRepairing shoes\, le
 ather\, or vinyl materials\n\nPerforming alterations \\(making garments bi
 gger/smaller\\)\n\nReplacing rivets/grommets\n\nHemming certain fabrics \\
 (stretchy fabric\, sleek/luxury fabrics e.g. prom dresses\\)\n\nIf you are
  in need of garment hemming\, we require that you please pin your garment 
 to the desired length before you arrive.\n\nJoin Us!\n\nDoes fixing things
  sound like a fun way to spend a Saturday afternoon?  Or want to help out
  in other ways?  We need you! Sign up here: https://www.reusealliance.org
 /rf-volunteer\n\n or email volunteer@reusealliance.org if you have any que
 stions.
LOCATION:Novato City Hall
URL:https://www.reusealliance.org/events/novato-repair-fair-2026
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
