BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Masters of Hawaiian Music: George Kahumoku Jr\, Led Kaapana\, Jeff
  Peterson
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T213000
UID:260918l3rdRQC_7EKH4cRQlJKY1w
DESCRIPTION:Experience the soulful sounds and rich traditions of Hawai‘i
  with three legendary masters of **slack key guitar**—George Kahumoku J
 r.\, Led Kaapana\, and Jeff Peterson.\n\nRooted in the 19th-century paniol
 o (Hawaiian cowboy) culture\, slack key is a uniquely Hawaiian open-tuning
  guitar style passed down through generations. These three acclaimed music
 ians bring together decades of tradition\, storytelling\, and virtuosic mu
 sicianship.
LOCATION:Sebastopol Community Cultural Center
URL:https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/masters-of-hawaiian-mus
 ic-george-kahumoku-jr-led-kaapana-jeff-peterson/19944096/2026-10-10T19
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Haunts & Handiwork: A Halloween Craft Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T183000
UID:260918bf3ucnPbZ02QyUarfTNlcg
DESCRIPTION:Long before plastic decorations and store-bought costumes\, Ha
 lloween celebrations were filled with handmade decorations\, paper crafts\
 , games\, and a little bit of mischief. Halloween parties were often intim
 ate gatherings filled with creative touches made by hand.\n\nInspired by t
 he traditions of Jack and Charmian London’s era\, guests will spend the 
 evening creating their own festive Halloween crafts using period-inspired 
 designs and materials. From spooky paper decorations to vintage-inspired k
 eepsakes\, participants will have the opportunity to embrace their creativ
 ity and take their handmade creations home.\n\nAll materials will be provi
 ded\, and light refreshments will be available.  This hands-on workshop i
 s designed with adults in mind and isn’t suitable for young children.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/events/halloween-crafts/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Plein Air Trees Up Close: A Day at Jack London Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T150000
UID:2609186vvY-qtzokGJfbamDcASGw
DESCRIPTION:Slow down and take a close-up look at the beautiful trees of J
 ack London State Park. Explore the details found up close—bark\, moss\, 
 knots\, cracks\, textures\, patterns\, and the subtle variations in color 
 and light that make each tree unique.\n\nStudents will spend time observin
 g and drawing aspects of the trees around them while learning and practici
 ng foundational observational drawing skills\, including proportion\, shap
 e\, line\, texture\, and composition.\n\nDiscover the meditative benefits 
 of a plein air art practice while spending meaningful time in nature and g
 aining a deeper appreciation for the beauty\, complexity\, and individuali
 ty of the trees all around. All levels of experience are welcome.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/events/plein-air-trees-october-10-2026/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Retos en las Montañas (Challenges in the Mountains)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T150000
UID:260917fTlnN6JkcECueaAriuR3xg
DESCRIPTION:Join Jack London Park Partners and Sonoma Ecology Center staff
  in a series of intermediate hikes\, guided in Spanish\, between Jack Lond
 on State Historic Park and Sugarloaf Ridge State Park. Each hike is a roun
 d trip\, returning to the starting point\, and will increase in length or 
 difficulty. Not appropriate for children under 12 years old.\n\n1.    
  Sat. Oct. 10 – Jack London's Ancient Redwood. 3.72 miles\, 620 ft. elev
 ation (meet at Jack London State Historic Park).\n\n2.     Sat. Oct. 1
 7 – Sugarloaf's waterfall loop. 2.39 miles\, 610 ft. elevation (meet at 
 Sugarloaf Ridge State Park).\n\n3.     Sat. Oct. 24 – Upper Fallen t
 o Camp Via to Fern Lake at Jack London. 5.72 miles\, 1\,150 ft. elevation 
 (meet at Jack London State Historic Park).\n\n4.     Sat. Nov. 7 – G
 unsight Rock at Sugarloaf/Hood Mountain Regional Park. 6.44 miles\, 2\,129
  ft. elevation (meet at Sugarloaf Ridge State Park).\n\n5.     Sun. No
 v. 15 – Sonoma Ridge in Sonoma Developmental Center/Jack London. 9.67 mi
 les\, 2\,126 ft. elevation (meet at the intersection of Arnold Dr. and Har
 ney Rd.\, inside the SDC).\n\n6.     Sat.  Nov. 21 – "The Big Loop"
  at Sugarloaf. 7.37 miles\, 1\,739 ft elevation (meet at Sugarloaf Ridge S
 tate Park).
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/reto2026
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
