BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Maple Magic & Winter Wonder
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T170000
UID:2608241iDuyX4NDUGW995vjbTdcw
DESCRIPTION:As the days grow shorter and cooler\, Sonoma Botanical Garden 
 transforms with the beauty of the changing seasons. From the first signs o
 f autumn in October to the brilliant display of rare Asian maples in Nov
 ember and the quiet beauty of early winter in December\, each visit offer
 s something new to discover. \n\n*Maple Magic* *& Winter Wonder* invites
  visitors to experience this special time of year through nature\, creativ
 ity\, and connection. Throughout the season\, the Garden offers guided wal
 ks\, hands-on workshops\, lectures\, and special experiences inspired by t
 he changing landscape. Wander among vibrant fall foliage\, breathe in the 
 sweet fragrance of katsura trees\, enjoy creative programs\, and experienc
 e the peaceful beauty of the Garden as it transitions into winter.
LOCATION:Sonoma Botanical Garden
URL:https://sonomabg.org/visit/maple-magic-winter-wonder/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Park Rx-Intermediate Hiking for Fitness Fall 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T130000
UID:260823Q6xTK1pK40-dr31Y2Nlpmg
DESCRIPTION:The program leaders will guide you on 8 weekly hikes
  with the challenge increasing each week. Leaders will have grou
 p discussions about gear\, hydration\, hiking poles\, first aid a
 nd pacing\, etc. The group's final hike aims for Bald Mountain\,
  where hikers can enjoy stunning vistas.\n\nThe following is a l
 ist of possible routes specifically selected for this hiking seri
 es: \n\n1\\) Sat 9/26 — Creekside \\+ Waterfall loop\, 3.6 mil
 es\, 750 ft elevation \\[meet @ White Barn\\] 2\\) Sat 10/03 –
  Vista Trail loop\, 3.4 miles\, 830 ft elevation \\[meet @ Whit
 e Barn\\] 3\\) Sat 10/10 – Hillside to Neptune table \\+ Meado
 w\, 4.4 miles\, 970 ft elevation \\[meet @ White Barn\\] 4\\) Sa
 t 10/17 – Goodspeed to Nattkemper bench\, 3.8 miles\, 1\,240 f
 t elevation \\[meet @ Goodspeed lot\\] 5\\) Sat 10/24 – Hillsid
 e \\+ Vista Trail loop\, 3.6 miles\, 1\,070 ft elevation \\[meet
  @ White Barn\\] 6\\) Sat 10/31 – False Lake Meadow & Lake I
 lsanjo loop in Trionne-Annadel SP\, 6.1 miles\, 670 ft elevation
  \\[meet @ Annadel's Cobblestone Trailhead\\] 7\\) Sat 11/07 – 
 Fern Lake \\+ Orchard loop in SDC/Jack London SHP\, 5.5 miles\,
  1\,460 ft elevation \\[meet @ Walnut & North St inside SDC\; 
 park on Grove St\\] 8\\) Sat 11/14 – Bald Mtn summit \\(w/opti
 onal Headwaters detour\, 5.8 miles\\)\, 5.1 miles\, 1\,670 ft ele
 vation \\[meet @ White Barn\\]\n\nPlease note these routes are su
 bject to change based on the group and weather\, as the group 
 does hike in light rains. Wear appropriate footwear for rocky or
  slippery trails\, and layers. Bring water\, and if desired\, a
  snack. The group will be limited to 35 participants. \n\nThe h
 iking series costs $80 \\(plus a $10 parking fee per visit. Not
 e that the Sugarloaf Annual Pass is $59 and valid at Sugarloaf
  and Jack London SHP\\)\, or free-of-cost for participants with 
 a September 2026 or newer Park Rx from a Sonoma County Medical
  Provider.
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/intfffall26
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Live Music Happy Hour - The Ukulele Ramblers - Open Uke Jam!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T180000
UID:260817x_Yypik3W0yqbQc4I4Z-Hg
DESCRIPTION:Saturday afternoons hit differently at Barrel Proof Lounge.\n\
 nWe open early — 3pm — and hand the room over to Ukulele Ramblers\, a 
 friendly\, talented ukulele collective that turns Happy Hour into a laid-b
 ack\, sing-along hang.\n\nThis is live music and an open uke jam. Bring yo
 ur ukulele if you’ve got one. Bring your voice even if you don’t. The 
 Ramblers lead the way with familiar tunes\, easy harmonies\, and a welcomi
 ng vibe that makes it just as fun to join in as it is to sit back and list
 en.\n\nNo pressure. No ego. Just good songs\, good people\, and a room tha
 t feels like it belongs to everyone.\n\n Live Music & Open Uke Jam | 3–
 6pm  Happy Hour drinks  Free popcorn  21+\n\n Barrel Proof Lounge 501 
 Mendocino Avenue\, Downtown Santa Rosa\n\nIt’s the kind of afternoon you
  plan to stop by for one drink… and somehow stay for three hours.\n\n**w
 ww.UkuleleRamblers.net**\n\nCheck out **www.BarrelProofLounge.com** for al
 l sorts of good times ahead!
LOCATION:Barrel Proof Lounge
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/live-music-happy-hour-the-ukulele-rambler
 s-open-uke-jam-tickets-1485589782029?aff=oddtdtcreator
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Andaz Hotel
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T000000
UID:2608137-FkrXA3QkKvCKbQT7qVMw
DESCRIPTION:Callie Watts is a singer/songwriter from Northern California w
 ho was raised on classical music\, The Beatles and The Beach Boys before d
 iscovering Joni Mitchell\, Elton John\, Stevie Wonder\, Paul Simon\, Billy
  Joel\, Carole King\, and all the great writers of the ’60s and 70’s w
 ho have influenced her sound and writing style. After graduating high scho
 ol\, Callie began playing and performing solo\, as well as in local and ba
 y area bands of different genres. She’s played blues with Eric Lindell a
 nd the Reds\, funky soul with Phatty\, and jazz/swing with Savoy Swingers 
 along with many other various projects. Callie has taken turns throughout 
 her career as a keyboardist\, guitarist\, writer\, and lead/backing vocali
 st\, and she’s currently a member of the dynamic Sonoma County funk rock
  band Burrows and Dilbeck\, having joined in 2010 as part of the former ba
 nd Frobeck. Over time\, she’s had the honor of opening for acts such as 
 Bootsy Collins\, Elvin Bishop\, Huey Lewis and The News\, War\, Ozomatli\,
  Bill Champlin\, Booker T\, and the B52s. Callie continues to perform freq
 uently as an acoustic solo artist\, focusing on developing a core audience
  and a buzz for her original material. Come hang out and listen at venues 
 such as Aroma Roasters\, Rincon Valley Tap Room and Bottle Shop\, and Hopm
 onk Tavern.
LOCATION:Andaz Napa - A Concept By Hyatt
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108590257?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
