BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:2026 Children's Jamboree & Marketplace
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261011T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261011T140000
UID:260906otW4vse0S0GlnQnlz-o_oQ
DESCRIPTION:**2026 Children's Jamboree & Marketplace - Come Grow\, Learn\,
  Play\, and Shop with Us!**\n\nThis fun\, free event for children and adul
 ts is Sunday\, October 11 from 11 a.m. to 2 p.m. at Nokhnoma Teaching and 
 Demonstration Garden in Santa Rosa.\n\n**Activities for children** will in
 clude items they can make and take home such as corn husk dolls\, sun catc
 hers\, gratitude banners\, seed pots\, garden art rocks\, and more! ﻿ 
 ﻿\n\n**Marketplace** will feature an assortment of 4-inch and 1-gallon s
 ucculents\, succulent containers\, succulent topped pumpkins in assorted s
 izes\, small and medium wreaths crafted with flora\, cones and/or succulen
 ts\, oyster shell succulents and decoupage oyster shell ornaments\, beaded
  light catchers\, and gardening books. All proceeds benefit the UC Master 
 Gardener Program of Sonoma County. Cash\, checks and credit cards accepted
 .\n\n**Information tables** will be staffed with Sonoma County Master Gard
 ener volunteers who will share home gardening information\, answer your ho
 me gardening-related questions and provide information about our programs 
 and projects.\n\n**Partner organizations** on site will include the Girl S
 couts\, Sonoma County Bee Association\, Children's Museum of Sonoma County
 \, Master Food Preservers\, Zero Waste\, Sonoma County 4-H\, and others.\n
 \nRegister to attend: Go to https://tinyurl.com/5dk8nw7r or sonomamg.ucanr
 .edu/ Upcoming Events to complete your registration. After registering\, 
 you will receive a confirmation email containing information about attendi
 ng the event.\n\n**General information**\n\nADA-compliant porta potty on s
 ite.\n\nADA parking will be available.\n\nWater available for filling wate
 r bottles.\n\nWear comfortable\, closed-toe shoes suitable for walking on 
 unpaved\, uneven paths\n\nBring a hat if desired.\n\nNo animals allowed\, 
 except trained service dogs.\n\nFood and beverages will not be available\,
  bring your own snacks or picnic lunch.
LOCATION:Nokhnoma Teaching and Demonstration Garden
URL:https://tinyurl.com/5dk8nw7r
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:SugarShuttle: Sugarloaf ↔ Hood Mtn\, Los Alamos Rd
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261011T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261011T115500
UID:260903kzaIk6opFkaUlxU166DuKQ
DESCRIPTION:How it works: Every hour\, our Shuttle will leave fro
 m either Sugarloaf Ridge State Park's Visitor Center\, making a 
 brief stop at the Goodspeed parking lot\, or Hood Mountain Regio
 nal Park’s Los Alamos Rd parking lot. Make a reservation to r
 ide to the other end of the trail and begin your hike\, or hi
 ke and ride back. We recommend riding first and hiking back to
  your car afterward—no worries about how long you take to fin
 ish your adventure. The hike should take 4 to 5 hours depending
  on your pace\; the distance is about 7.5 miles one-way with a
 pproximately 2\,500ft of elevation gain. \n\nBring at least 64 oz
  of water\, sun protection \\(the majority of the trail is expo
 sed\\)\, a good paper map \\(some of the trail signs on Hood M
 tn Regional Park are still damaged from the 2020 wildfire and t
 rails might not be well marked\\)\, and if desired\, hiking pole
 s\, a lunch\, and a friend.\n\nIf you are riding from Sugarloaf\
 , the Goodspeed lot fills up quickly. If it is full\, please p
 ark at the main lot and pick up the shuttle at the Visitor Ce
 nter \\(you will have to hike a mile back to the main lot fro
 m the bottom of the canyon/Goodspeed lot\\). Remember\, the Hood
  Mountain pick-up is at the end of Los Alamos Road: 3000 Los 
 Alamos Rd\, Santa Rosa\, CA\, 94509. Los Alamos Rd is a windy\,
  narrow\, sometimes one-lane\, 5-mile road without cell reception
 —allow time to get to the lot \\(NOT the Pythian Rd lot\\). 
 Please note there are currently no restrooms\, water\, or cell s
 ervice at this trailhead.  \n\nRegistration is required as there
  is only space for 6 riders at a time\, but you can ride on
  a space-available basis as well. There is no charge for the r
 ide\, the $10 reservation fee is refunded on site the day of t
 he event\, unless you choose to donate it to keep this service
  running. Dogs and bikes are not allowed in the shuttle or on
  Goodspeed Trail \\(the State Park portion of the hiking route\\
 ). Parking fees apply.
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/2026octsatshuttle
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
