DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261011T170000
UID:260529fWz836spCEOTnGQOgajmwg
DESCRIPTION:Twist of Fate\n\nOctober 10\, 11 & 12\, 2026\n\nWeill Hall\, G
 reen Music Center\n\n**Francesco Lecce-Chong\,** conductor\n\n**Maxim Land
 o\,** piano\n\n**MATT BROWNE:** Divertimento for Orchestra (World Premiere
 ) **FRANZ LISZT:** Concerto No. 1 in E-Flat major for Piano and Orchestra\
 , S.124 **PYOTR ILYICH TCHAIKOVSKY:** Symphony No. 4 in F minor\, Opus 36\
 n\nThe season’s opener begins with a fanfare of fate\, which marks a poi
 gnant full circle for Francesco Lecce-Chong. He returns to the first piece
  he led with the Symphony: Tchaikovsky’s tempestuous Symphony No. 4. Thi
 s high-octane program also features fiery virtuoso Maxim Lando in Liszt’
 s thrilling Piano Concerto No. 1 and a world premiere by Matt Browne\, a c
 elebrated alumnus of the First Symphony Project.\n\n**Programs\, dates\, a
 rtists\, and prices are subject to change without notice. Tickets are subj
 ect to availability.**\n\nPhoto by Chris McGuire
LOCATION:Green Music Center
URL:https://www.srsymphony.org/event/twist-of-fate/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
