UID:260419Bhgq5P8a00eFYo4r_iJiTw
DESCRIPTION:Every Sunday: Free\, live jazz every week performed by some of
  the best musicians in the SF Bay Area and beyond\, right in the heart of 
 downtown Petaluma! Every Sunday from 1 to 3:30\, local jazz bassist and mu
 sic book publisher Chuck Sher presents a rotating ensemble of professional
 \, veteran jazz musicians in Putnam Plaza Park\, right next to the Speakea
 sy. In partnership with Music in Place\, Jamey Aebersold Jazz Books\, JamB
 ar\, and MadCap Labs\, this event started in 2020 and has since become a s
 taple for locals and visitors alike. Stop by and enjoy some of the best ja
 zz the Bay Area has to offer!
LOCATION:Putnam Plaza Park
URL:https://www.facebook.com/jazzintheplazapetaluma
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Slave Play - a Left Edge Theatre Production
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261011T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261011T150000
UID:260924JqgaQvvyJUGbgbIZK3CvJw
DESCRIPTION:Presented by Left Edge Theatre. At the MacGregor Plantation\, 
 the antebellum South collides with the present in a provocative fever drea
 m where race\, desire\, gender\, and power intertwine. Nothing is quite as
  it seems-and yet everything is. Jeremy O. Harris's explosive\, award-winn
 ing Slave Play rips apart the boundaries between history and modern Americ
 a\, confronting the enduring legacy of slavery and the complex intersectio
 ns of race\, gender\, and sexuality. Recommended for ages 17\\+. Contains 
 nudity\, sexual content\, simulated sexual violence\, and racially violent
  language. TICKETS ZONE A \\(Close to the action\\) $45 ZONE B \\(Middle o
 f the house\\) $35 ZONE C \\(In the back\\) $25 Tickets at Door - $45 - So
  buy in advance! SPECIAL DATES Thu 9/25: OPENING NIGHT & PARTY - Stick aro
 und to celebrate after the show! Wed 9/30: Industry Night - Calling all th
 eatre people! All tickets $20. Thur 10/1: Discount night - $10 off all tic
 kets Advance purchase strongly encouraged.
LOCATION:The California
URL:https://creativesonoma.org/event/slave-play-a-left-edge-theatre-produc
 tion/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:John Prine Tribute with David Luning\, Jason Crosby\, Ben Dubin an
 d Victoria George
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261011T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261011T200000
UID:260923TKb33RQi2E-rS0yFlHEz5A
DESCRIPTION:David Luning returns to OCA for a special tribute celebrating 
 John Prine's birthday. David will be joined by musical colleagues Jason Cr
 osby\, Ben Dubin and Victoria George. Tickets are $35\, $30 for OCA member
 s.  Get Tickets This show will take place in our auditorium. Doors open at
  5:30 PM. David Luning knew at a young age the path his life should take. 
 Throughout generations\, troubadours and singers have harnessed the cultur
 al landscape and passed it along\, with the likes of John Prine and Townes
  Van Zandt paving the way with the telling of their stories. Following in 
 those footsteps\, the 29-year-old Sonoma County singer/songwriter's new re
 cord is the product of a massive turn in his life and taps into that cultu
 ral archive. Listening to ‘Souvenirs' by John Prine\, was a cornerstone 
 moment\, compelling Luning to leave Berklee College and follow in the trad
 ition of these iconic troubadours.
LOCATION:Occidental Center for the Arts
URL:https://www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org/upcoming-events/david-lunin
 g-friends
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Workshop: Off the Grid Printing
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261011T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261011T130000
UID:260819AifIp1HrdE68Aqk_VQZg0w
DESCRIPTION:In this two day workshop\, students will work hands-on with me
 tal and wood type to create off-grid compositions-playing with spacing\, r
 otation\, fragmentation\, overlap\, and improvisation. We'll explore how i
 mbalance\, disruption\, and intuition can shape meaning\, rhythm\, and vis
 ual impact in printed work. This class emphasizes process over perfection.
  Expect to test ideas\, make quick prints\, respond to chance\, and let th
 e material qualities of type and press guide the work. Suitable for curiou
 s beginners and experienced printers alike\, this workshop offers a suppor
 tive space to experiment\, loosen habits\, and discover new possibilities 
 in letterpress printing beyond the grid. All materials provided. No prior 
 letterpress experience required\, though comfort with basic printing conce
 pts is helpful.
LOCATION:D
URL:https://creativesonoma.org/event/workshop-off-the-grid-printing/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Meet + Greet: More Trouble Than It's Worth by Lisa Moore Ramee
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261011T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261011T120000
UID:2608164R22eLiG10mhTfaGFcrnSg
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a special meet-and-greet event with Lisa Moore Ram
 ee\, author of More Trouble Than It's Worth. This event is free\, but we a
 ppreciate your RSVP below so we can plan for your attendance. ABOUT THE BO
 OK "Ramée successfully weaves themes of friendship\, sports\, social resp
 onsibility\, and family into this engaging coming-of-age story. Shayla’s
  journal features quotations from famous Black women\, a seamless way of s
 haring the insights she gains with readers...A lively novel that explores 
 the inner conflicts and group dynamics that tweens often reckon with." —
  Kirkus Reviews From award-winning author Lisa Moore Ramée comes the comp
 anion to A Good Kind of Trouble\, a heartfelt and powerful sequel about co
 ming of age\, social justice\, and the trials of friendship and competitio
 n\, in which Shayla will learn the true definition of “personal best.”
  After a hard seventh-grade year full of misunderstandings\, face plants\,
  and bullies\, all Shayla wants is a hassle-free summer. Her ticket to a s
 ummer of fun? Joining the club track team! However\, Shayla struggles to f
 it in with new friends\, to set a personal best that will secure her a spo
 t in the exclusive Junior Olympics\, and reluctantly earns the title of 
 “Prank Queen.” But Shayla discovers that sometimes trying so hard to s
 tay out of trouble ends up making things a whole lot worse. Will she risk 
 new friendships by owning up to a big mistake? And is she ready to speak o
 ut against another social injustice? In this powerful and heartfelt follow
 -up to A Good Kind of Trouble from acclaimed author Lisa Moore Ramée\, Sh
 ayla will learn the true definition of personal best. ABOUT THE AUTHOR Lis
 a Moore Ramée was born and raised in Los Angeles and now lives in Norther
 n California with her husband\, daughter\, obnoxious cat\, and rambunctiou
 s \\(but sweet\\) dog. She's a devout believer in dreams coming true and i
 s the author of A Good Kind of Trouble\, a Walter Dean Myers Honor Book\, 
 The Everybody Experiment\, Something to Say\, and MapMaker. You can visit 
 her online at lisamooreramee.com.
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/27815061771469203/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
