UID:260903WUns1TL85EOeSNRHlyYO6Q
DESCRIPTION:This September and October\, **Lucci Lambrusco is taking over
  Golden Hour at El Dorado Kitchen**\, bringing a taste of Italian aperi
 tivo culture to the patio all season long.\n\nSettle in for a late afterno
 on of Lucci Lambrusco\, Italian wines\, cocktails and shareable bites made
  for lingering. Throughout the two-month takeover\, Lucci will be joined e
 very Thursday by a rotating lineup of guest wineries\, importers and produ
 cers\, each stopping by to pour something special and share a little more 
 about what’s in your glass.\n\nThe season kicks off on **Thursday\, Sep
 tember 3**\, with live music\, Lucci Lambrusco\, passed pizzas and arancin
 i on the patio.\n\n**LUCCI ITALIAN GOLDEN HOUR TAKEOVER** Monday–Frid
 ay | 3:00–5:00 PM September & October\n\n**THURSDAY GUEST WINE SERIES** 
 Every Thursday | 3:00–5:00 PM\n\nSeptember 3 | Lucci Lambrusco\n\nSeptem
 ber 10 | Oliver McCrum Wines\n\nSeptember 17 | Mora Estate\n\nSeptember 24
  | Idlewild Wines\n\nOctober 1 | Cline Family Cellars\n\nOctober 8 | Unti 
 Vineyards\n\nOctober 15 | Massican\n\n...and more to come!\n\n**Lucci is p
 ouring all season long\, with a few friends joining along the way.**\n\nCo
 me for a glass. Stay for another.\n\n**JOIN US FOR GOLDEN HOUR**
LOCATION:El Dorado Hotel
URL:https://eldoradosonoma.com/el-dorado-kitchen/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Beginner Salsa - Tuesdays
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261013T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261013T183000
UID:260705qVKCPNeOhk2n10GCVz8A8A
DESCRIPTION:Ready to dance? Join our beginner salsa class where no experie
 nce or partner is needed. Just comfortable shoes and desire to have fun!\n
 \nGreat for first timers!\n\nNo dance experience required\n\nNon-marking s
 hoes soles\n\nNo partner necessary\n\nOur relaxed environment is perfect f
 or learning salsa basics\, as we make it fun and enjoyable. In this class 
 you will learn basic directional steps\, proper frame for partner-work and
  simple turn patterns. We organize our curriculum so that the movements ar
 e easy to remember. Join us to learn the fundamentals! No experience is ne
 cessary and no partner is required. Drop-in fee is $20.\n\nDate & Time: Tu
 esdays @ 5:30PM – 6:30PM\n\nAddress: 4140 Redwood Highway \\#8 San Rafae
 l\, CA\n\nNote: Arrive 10 minutes before. No floor marking shoe soles allo
 wed.
LOCATION:Salsa Dance Marin
URL:https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/beginner-salsa-tuesdays
 /17157360/2026-10-13T17
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Intermediate Salsa Class
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261013T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261013T200000
UID:260704Lndom3mrjkOyTtsUJbQ7bA
DESCRIPTION:This class is designed for dancers who have a solid grasp of t
 he basics and are eager to expand their repertoire with more complex and f
 luid movements.\n\nPre- requisite:\n\nSalsa Class Beginners\n\nEach week\,
  we’ll break down a new move\, focusing on the technique and connection 
 that will make you a more confident and stylish dancer. We’ll go beyond 
 the foundational steps to cover a wide range of essential intermediate pat
 terns and styling\, including:\n\nTurns and Spins:\n\nMaster your inside a
 nd outside turns\, double spins\, and the elegant 360 and Hand Toss moves.
 \n\nIntricate Patterns:\n\nLearn to execute the 360\, wrap\, as well as va
 rious Cross Body Lead variations like the U-Turn and Spiral.\n\nFootwork a
 nd Styling:\n\nEnhance your rhythm and flair with advanced footwork like t
 he Suzy Q\, Front Tap\, and Mambo Step. We’ll also work on styling with 
 a wrap and improving your posture and upper body movement.\n\nThis class i
 s your chance to refine your technique\, improve your lead-follow connecti
 on\, and add a variety of fun and dynamic moves to your salsa vocabulary. 
 Join us and elevate your dance!\n\nDetails:\n\nNo partner necessary — ro
 tations ensure everyone gets to dance.\n\nPlease wear non-marking shoe so
 les to protect the floor.\n\nArrive 10 minutes early to warm up and get s
 ettled.\n\nDate & Time: Tuesdays @ 7:00 pm – 8:00 PM
LOCATION:Salsa Dance Marin
URL:https://salsadancemarin.com/salsa-class-intermediate-tuesday/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Classic Cinema - Where the Crawdads Sing
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261013T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261013T200500
UID:260627fbdhvOgQokCTaVeLZb9-zA
DESCRIPTION:Tuesday\, October 13\, 2026\n\n6:00pm    Doors open 5:30 pm\
 n\nFree entry. Donations greatly appreciated.\n\nConcessions open for purc
 hase.\n\nAssistive listening devices available.\n\n Sponsored by Nancy an
 d Grant Jordan\n\nWhere the Crawdads Sing tells the story of Kya\, a girl 
 who was left alone and grew up by herself in the dangerous marshlands of N
 orth Carolina. For years\, rumors about the "Marsh Girl" scared the people
  of Barkley Cove\, keeping the smart and strong Kya apart from her communi
 ty. When she becomes close to two young men from town\, Kya steps into a n
 ew and surprising world\; but when one of them is found dead\, the communi
 ty quickly blames her as the main suspect. As the case goes on\, it become
 s harder to know what really happened\, threatening to uncover many secret
 s hidden in the marsh.\n\n Released Jul 15\, 2022\n\nDrama\, Mystery & T
 hriller\n\nRuntime 2h 5m\n\nPG-13 \\(Sexual Content\, A Sexual Assault\, S
 ome Violence\\)
LOCATION:Soper-Reese Theatre
URL:http://soperreesetheatre.com
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
