BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Antarctica: The Frozen Desert | Photographs by Vegar Abelsnes
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261013T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261013T170000
UID:260914WK0ZiR6_tkyj56X_Gyde9g
DESCRIPTION:1st Street Gallery at WTRSHD will present *“Antarctica: The 
 Frozen Desert\,”* a new body of fine art photography by Vegar Abelsnes\,
  opening September 26th\, 2026\, and on view September through November. 
  The exhibition marks a deliberate turn in Abelsnes’ photography\; after
  more than two decades of working in a commercial and advertising capacity
 \, he has embarked on a career as a photo and field guide in the polar reg
 ions. The exhibit features work generated over 6 *voyages to the* Antarcti
 c Peninsula. He is returning to Antarctica in January and will add the Fal
 klands and South Georgia to his list of destinations to guide and photogra
 ph.\n\nTraveling to some of the most remote and inhospitable coastlines on
  Earth\, Abelsnes has photographed a landscape that exists almost entirely
  outside of human time. The ice in these images began forming millions of 
 years ago\, while Homo sapiens have only existed for roughly 300\,000 year
 s. Defined by such a scale\, Antarctica is less a place than a record — 
 vast\, indifferent\, treacherous\, and staggeringly beautiful\, holding a 
 kind of cosmic truth that Abelsnes says is more important now than ever be
 fore.
LOCATION:1st Street Gallery @ WTRSHD
URL:https://vegarabelsnes.com/ANTARCTICA:-The-Frozen-Desert/thumbs
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Raw & Rogue
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261013T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261013T210000
UID:260912ao_EHDrHSEKsu2N5sv5ZnQ
DESCRIPTION:For three Tuesdays this fall\, Raw \\+ Rogue brings an intimat
 e twelve-seat omakase experience to the rooftop of Appellation Healdsburg.
  Across twelve courses\, Chef Willer Larreal Perez—a Venezuela-born chef
  trained at omakase counters in Los Angeles and Miami—builds each dish a
 round the fish\, taking guests on a scenic culinary journey from the count
 er to the plate. An amuse opens the experience and dessert brings it to a 
 close\, while wine pairings from Baron Ziegler\, co-founder of Healdsburg
 ’s Banshee Wines and founder of Marine Layer\, move alongside the menu. 
 Each course is paired with its own song\, creating a soundtrack that build
 s plate by plate as the light shifts over Northern Sonoma County. Together
 \, the food\, wine and music create a multisensory evening designed to unf
 old in rhythm with the rooftop setting. \n\nWhen: Tuesdays | September 29
 \, October 13\, October 27 \\(6:30 pm\\) \n\nPrice: $295 per guest\, wine
  selections prices separately \n\nReservations are available through Open
 Table: Raw & Rogue \n\nPre-paid reservations are required.
LOCATION:Appellation Healdsburg
URL:https://beelinerooftop.getbento.com/event/raw-rogue/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:California Native Creations Art Show
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261013T083000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261013T163000
UID:260909o48jOdxenUKsNmruT_EtEA
DESCRIPTION:**September is the 17th Annual Pomo Honoring Month.** On Monda
 y\, Sept. 14\, the 6th California Native Creations Art Show opens Person S
 enior Wing\, Finley Community Center\, 2060 W. College Ave.\, Santa Rosa\,
  CA. The show is free and open to the public Monday – Friday\, 8:30 a.m.
 -4:30 p.m.\, through November 19.\n\nThe established and up-and-coming nat
 ive artists create with digital media\, paint and traditional materials in
  their art\, weaving\, regalia\, beadwork\, jewelry\, baskets and quilts.
  The artists include:\n\n·         Meyo Marrufo\, painter\, gues
 t curator for the de Young Museum and the Sonoma Valley Art Museum\,\n\n·
          Buffie Campbell\, Vice Chair\, Sherwood Valley Rancheria\
 , cultural teacher and master basket maker\,\n\n·         Henry E
 dward Frank\, *Yurok/Kashaya Pomo*\, who will show paintings and work with
  Legos titled *Mind Prison\,*\n\n·         Digital artist Nicolas
  (Nico) Vargas\, *Kashia Band of Pomo Indians*\, whose art was featured at
  the 55th Annual Stanford Powwow.\n\n·         plus Gloria Carret
 ero\; Rose Hammock\; Rudy Hammock\; Jocelyn Garcia\; Arella Ortega LaRose\
 , *Kashia Band of Pomo Indians*\; Angelica Smith\, *Manchester Point Arena
  and Yokayo Rancheria*\; Maria Pasalo\; Michelle Napoli\; Martina Morgan\,
  *Kashia Band of Pomo Indians*\; Hands Lopez\; Shashoni Hanover-Redenbaug
 h\; Katie Williams-Elliott\, Juan Partida\, and Mia Pasalo\, *Big Valley P
 omo Tribe*.
LOCATION:Person Senior Wing\, Finley Community Center
URL:http://www.pomoproject.org/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Live Music Happy Hour - The Hutchinsons: Sonoma Seasoned Americana
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261013T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261013T190000
UID:260906Rp5XEdk8OEqpvXtCc0EKZA
DESCRIPTION:For people who like to party...but want to be home at a reason
 able hour...\n\nThe Hutchinsons: Seasoned Americana - Every 1st Tuesday! C
 oming from the tradition of folk music\, Kevin Hutchinson is a musical sto
 ryteller. His influences and styles cover many genres: folk\, folk rock\, 
 blues\, rock\, rockabilly\, Americana\, country\, swing\, and\, of course\
 , folk. His music is lyric driven\, and spans topics from love to social c
 ommentary\, serious to light hearted.\n\nKevin loves connecting with the a
 udience with his originals and thoughtful covers of artists that have insp
 ired him\, often pulling from their lesser known material.\n\nArtistic inf
 luences\, covering decades\, include: John Prine\; Bob Dylan\; Bruce Cockb
 urn\; Warren Zevon\; Crosby\, Stills and Nash\; Peter\, Paul and Mary\; Ro
 bert Earl Keen\; Tom Russel\; Tom Paxton\; Paul Thorne\; and many more.\n\
 n21+ Happy Hour Pricing 4-7pm All beers - $6 + $2 off wine. Live Music 5-7
 pm 2 drink minimum\, please\n\nCheck out **www.BarrelProofLounge.com** for
  all sorts of good times ahead!
LOCATION:Barrel Proof Lounge
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/live-music-happy-hour-the-hutchinsons-son
 oma-seasoned-americana-tickets-1336190193839?aff=oddtdtcreator
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
