  The Abbey\, Wed\, Oct 14\, 6-8:30\n\n1st time with this exact lineup! Cou
 ld be wild!... with Dallis Craft\, Tim Eschliman\, Mark Larson\, Bowen Bro
 wn and special guest Peter Siegel (Commander Cody Band) on pedal steel... 
 Soulful Roots Rock\, R&B and Twangishnes: New Copasetics at Peacetown Cont
 inues... Hopmonk Sebastopol In The Abbey\, Wed\, Oct 14\, 6-8:30\n\nTheir 
 repertoire extends from originals to their own take on select material fro
 m great artists such as The Band\, Gary Nicholson\, Arthur Alexander\, Ric
 hard Thompson\, Buddy & Julie Miller\, Lucinda Williams\, Taj Mahal\, Dan 
 Hicks\, NRBQ\, Manual Galban\, Doris Troy\, Ike & Tina Turner\, ...Hank Wi
 lliams\n\nyes\, ay 230 Petaluma Ave Sebastopol\, CA 95472 (707) 829-7300\n
 \n"...this is roots Americana of a high order... there's plenty of good st
 uff in such genres as soul\, rockabilly\, country and get this\, 1970s Eng
 lish pub rock... Twang-Ucopia is very much a bunch of mates having a good 
 time knocking out their set live in the studio with minimal overdubs..." -
  David Osler\, Blues Matters Mag\n\n"Roots rockabilly from a wily crew wit
 h a load of credits ... Whether kicking it out on originals or covers\, th
 ey understand the genre and the groove and deliver accordingly and appropr
 iately."\n\n\\- Midwest Record Recap\, Twang-ucopia (Balanced Diet) by New
  Copasetics\n\nsee also http://www.newcopasetics.com\n\nhear the album: ht
 tps://orcd.co/7ogareg\n\nCDs & LPs at http://www.globerecords.com & discog
