BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Addams Family Musical
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261015T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261015T220000
UID:260914oJ-Yp1ElMUeycQwrJ9iieA
DESCRIPTION:San Marin Performing Arts is kicking off the 2026–27 season 
 with The Addams Family\, a delightfully spooky musical coming to the Emily
  Gates Performing Arts Center\n\nJust in time for Halloween\, this family-
 friendly production brings the famously eccentric Addams family to the sta
 ge in a story filled with humor\, heart\, memorable music and plenty of wo
 nderfully macabre fun. In The Addams Family\, Wednesday Addams has grown u
 p—and fallen in love with a sweet\, smart young man from a perfectly “
 normal” family. When she invites him and his parents to dinner\, Wednesd
 ay asks Gomez to keep a secret from Morticia\, setting off a hilarious cha
 in of events that turns one unforgettable evening upside down.\n\nFamily f
 riendly show!\n\nOUR STUDENT CAST\n\nGomez Addams — Kaden Hockinson\n\nM
 orticia Addams — Cami Cabrera\n\nWednesday Addams — Aaliyah Ortiz\n\nP
 ugsley Addams — Rosie Chi\n\nUncle Fester — Rogan Ferrell Bell\n\nGran
 dma Addams — Lenore Schulz\n\nLurch — Wyatt Mathyssen\n\nLucas Beineke
  — Skyler Viola\n\nMal Beineke — Tobias Mossberger\n\nAlice Beineke 
 — Clara Rose\n\nThe Ancestors — Hannah Yako\, Ella Blok\, Kody Kong\, 
 Noemy Pineda Montiel\, Dasha Hirai\, Maya Geere\, Sophia Gomez
LOCATION:Emily Gates Performing Arts Center
URL:https://www.sanmarinperformingarts.org/news-highlights/the-addams-fami
 ly
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Alborosie
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261015T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261015T200000
UID:260913cN681ijZ0E2sbTXwFHJRbQ
DESCRIPTION:Alberto Dascola aka Alborosie is an Italian reggae singer\, de
 ejay and producer based in Kingston\, Jamaica. He was born in Sicily in 19
 77 and in 1993\, he formed a reggae band in Italy called Reggae National T
 ickets. He produced his biggest hit ‘Herbalist’ in 2006 and notably re
 leased several other singles as ‘Kingston Town’ \, ‘Rastafari Anthem
 ’\, ‘Slam Bam’\, ‘Life’ featuring Jah Cure and ‘Call Up Jah’
  all on his own label Forward records.
LOCATION:Mystic Theatre & Music Hall
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/1039903574?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=2
 87&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cooper Kenward
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261015T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261015T180000
UID:260910wKfz7fwBDku-Yl5Y4b6Y4g
DESCRIPTION:Cooper Kenward writes warm feel-good-even-if-you-feel-bad song
 s. Hailing from a small town in Northern California\, he explores the odd 
 backroads of the heart. He has a mix of songs that could be blasted from a
  barn\, giggled from a ferris wheel\, or hummed in a rainstorm. By day\, K
 enward makes films. Some say that’s why his ballads smack of vivid detai
 ls. He honed his skills playing in the infamous garage band Nature’s Veg
 as in San Francisco\, and now resides in LA with his pitbull Bonnie Raitt.
LOCATION:Little Saint
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/1039474025?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=2
 87&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sister Sadie
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261015T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261015T200000
UID:260910BruXfLW5JUG6VGsH8sj2ow
DESCRIPTION:There was no master plan. No label strategy. Just a spontaneou
 s jam at Nashville’s Station Inn between a few friends\; seasoned player
 s\, all women\, making a little noise. But something clicked. The room lit
  up\, the crowd roared and Sister Sadie was born.\n\nWhat started as an ac
 cidental band became a force. GRAMMY-nominated. IBMA-decorated. Opry-valid
 ated. But for all the accolades\, they were often reduced to one line: an 
 all-female bluegrass band. True. But never the point. Sister Sadie has alw
 ays been about the music. The fire. The truth.\n\nTheir new album\, All Wi
 ll Be Well\, is that truth - loud\, fearless and free. You’ll hear echoe
 s of bluegrass\, but what rises is something bigger: country\, Americana w
 ith muscle\, gospel grit and raw storytelling.\n\nFrom the haunting “Pro
 digal Daughter” to the swagger of “Do What You Want” and the aching 
 beauty of “If I Don’t Have You\,” these six women are not performing
  roles\, they’re telling you who they are.\n\nThis is Sister Sadie\, evo
 lved: bold\, bonded and braver than ever. They're not asking for space. Th
 ey're taking it. And they’re just getting started.
LOCATION:HopMonk Tavern
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/1039796169?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=2
 87&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Joseph Hooker: Sonoma Valley’s Soldier\, Gambler\, & Farmer
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261015T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261015T201500
UID:260909K8GQFJa4iE6-GmAfBqJ2qg
DESCRIPTION:Joseph Hooker is remembered in history as a complex and highly
  controversial military figure. Understanding his past helps explain his f
 uture and his decisions.\n\nBefore gaining national fame as the commander 
 of the Union’s famous Army of the Potomac\, he faced both professional a
 nd personal struggles in Sonoma Valley\, many of which he caused himself. 
 During his time in Sonoma\, his well-known ego\, brashness\, and questiona
 ble dealings led to a series of costly mistakes that would follow him into
  the Civil War.\n\nJoin us for a fascinating presentation by author Travis
  P. Wagner. He will share new information on “Fighting Joe” Hooker’s
  turbulent years in Sonoma Valley. His talk will explore the complex man b
 ehind the myth. It will cover his time as a military officer\, a high-stak
 es gambler\, and a struggling frontier farmer\, before he achieved fame in
  the Civil War.\n\nTravis P. Wagner is a Professor Emeritus at the Univers
 ity of Southern Maine. He earned his Ph.D. from The George Washington Univ
 ersity. Dr. Wagner has written numerous articles on the history of America
 n industry\, environmental policy\, and technology. His eighth book\, Mili
 tary Honor on Trial: The Saga of Joseph Hooker and George H. Derby\, was p
 ublished by Sequoia Grove Press in August.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center - Community Room 110
URL:https://sonomavalleyhistory.org/event/joseph-hooker-sonoma-valleys-sol
 dier-gambler-farmer/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Golden Hour
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261015T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261015T170000
UID:260903c9cCqAIXP0eTgCg5crlInA
DESCRIPTION:This September and October\, **Lucci Lambrusco is taking over
  Golden Hour at El Dorado Kitchen**\, bringing a taste of Italian aperi
 tivo culture to the patio all season long.\n\nSettle in for a late afterno
 on of Lucci Lambrusco\, Italian wines\, cocktails and shareable bites made
  for lingering. Throughout the two-month takeover\, Lucci will be joined e
 very Thursday by a rotating lineup of guest wineries\, importers and produ
 cers\, each stopping by to pour something special and share a little more 
 about what’s in your glass.\n\nThe season kicks off on **Thursday\, Sep
 tember 3**\, with live music\, Lucci Lambrusco\, passed pizzas and arancin
 i on the patio.\n\n**LUCCI ITALIAN GOLDEN HOUR TAKEOVER** Monday–Frid
 ay | 3:00–5:00 PM September & October\n\n**THURSDAY GUEST WINE SERIES** 
 Every Thursday | 3:00–5:00 PM\n\nSeptember 3 | Lucci Lambrusco\n\nSeptem
 ber 10 | Oliver McCrum Wines\n\nSeptember 17 | Mora Estate\n\nSeptember 24
  | Idlewild Wines\n\nOctober 1 | Cline Family Cellars\n\nOctober 8 | Unti 
 Vineyards\n\nOctober 15 | Massican\n\n...and more to come!\n\n**Lucci is p
 ouring all season long\, with a few friends joining along the way.**\n\nCo
 me for a glass. Stay for another.\n\n**JOIN US FOR GOLDEN HOUR**
LOCATION:El Dorado Hotel
URL:https://eldoradosonoma.com/el-dorado-kitchen/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
