BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Home Ground Habitats Fall Celebration: Native Plant Sale and Tabli
 ng Event!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T150000
UID:260916re1WL-RpfEWUBOxLXu29SA
DESCRIPTION:On Saturday\, October 17\, from 10:00am-3:00pm\, Home Ground H
 abitats will have our annual Fall Celebration to kick off the planting sea
 son.\n\nCome celebrate with us at our open garden\, tabling event\, and fa
 ll plant sale! Fall is the best time of year to purchase native plants bec
 ause the start of California’s rainy season is the ideal time to add new
  plants to the garden. Planting with the first rains gives roots the cool\
 , wet winter months to settle in and become established before the warmer\
 , drier seasons arrive. Shop 20% off all habitat plants\, wildflower seeds
 \, and more - give your garden a strong start for the year ahead.\n\nHome 
 Ground Habitats is a native plant nursery\, demonstration garden\, and edu
 cation center located in Indian Valley\, Novato\, CA. As a community-cente
 red organization\, we focus on environmental education\, California native
  plant propagation\, and ethical land stewardship on nearly one acre of la
 nd. The demonstration gardens at Home Ground showcase a sustainable\, orga
 nic approach to creating a truly California-friendly landscape using nativ
 e plants and drought-tolerant Mediterranean species to increase biodiversi
 ty. We have native plant experts who can help anyone find the right plants
  to create a wildlife habitat garden in their own backyard. Our mission is
  to bring the natural world\, pollinators\, and wildlife to a landscape th
 at also provides sustenance for humans.\n\nAs we celebrate the shifting of
  the season\, our tabling event will offer information and educational res
 ources about bringing biodiversity into your garden\, supporting wildlife\
 , creating beautiful pollinator habitats\, and protecting the land around 
 us. Expect to see our amazing community partners: Marin County Parks\, Mar
 in Monarch Working Group\, Happy Bat Solutions\, Pesticide Free Zone\, Pol
 linator Partnership\, California Bluebird Recovery Program\, Museum of Ame
 rican Indian\, and WildCare. Presentations will be scheduled throughout th
 e day for even more learning.\n\nGet your garden ready and plant it out wi
 th habitat plants that support pollinators and wildlife from Home Ground H
 abitats! RSVP to let us know you're coming. https://homegroundhabitats.org
 /event/fall-celebration-plant-sale-at-home-ground-habitats/
LOCATION:Home Ground Habitats
URL:https://homegroundhabitats.org/event/fall-celebration-plant-sale-at-ho
 me-ground-habitats/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
