BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Book Launch With Sonoma County Author Karen Gebbia
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T130000
UID:260924XOqiqQ9orkWZJ93aBroeuA
DESCRIPTION:**You can't rush real iced tea.** Charlotte wants to wait pati
 ently. She really does. But waiting is hard\, especially on a stifling Mar
 yland morning\, when her t-shirt feels like a hot\, heavy blanket\, and sh
 e can't think of anything but Nana's cold\, sweet\, lemony\, real iced tea
 .\n\nThere are so many steps to Nana's secret recipe tea! Steeping\, sugar
 ing\, cooling . . . baking muffins to go with it! Nana tells her to find s
 omething useful to do while she waits\, so Charlotte sweeps\, and swings\,
  and snaps pillowcases\, but it still isn't ready!\n\nCharlotte has to fin
 d more things to do to pass the time\, and soon she finds that a day spent
  waiting can be a day spent enjoying the slower moments. Sometimes the swe
 etest things in life are the things we have to wait for\, and learning to 
 savor them slowly is a joy all its own. Included is a reader's note for ad
 ults on helping kids learn how to wait and a secret recipe to try at home.
 \n\nScavenger Hunt and Stickers for the kiddos.
LOCATION:Russian River Books & Letters
URL:https://www.booksletters.com/events/book-launch-with-sonoma-county-aut
 hor-karen-gebbia
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:ART TRAILS 2026 at the Art & Music Gallery in Petaluma
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T170000
UID:260923FMEaiP-u1E-ImXsCnJ7WrA
DESCRIPTION:Carol Tacconi and Corry Dastur are coming to the Art & Music G
 allery in Petaluma.\n\nA dynamic mix of abstract and post-impressionism wi
 thin the Art & Music Gallery's elegant\, spacious home.  See Studios 87A 
 & 87B in the Art Trails catalog.\n\nGet your copy of the catalog now.  Fi
 nd it around town for free\, or visit sonomaarttrails.org and view online.
    We hope to see you at the Art and Music Gallery.
LOCATION:Art and Music Gallery
URL:https://artandmusicgallery.com/events/art-trails/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:No Cell Sundays: Callie Watts & Kris Dilbeck
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T143000
UID:260922ZeW7DmYDukSOwrSAAsvx5Q
DESCRIPTION:Callie Watts: Where Classic Sounds Meet Modern Soul\n\nJoin us
  for No Cell Sundays with Callie Watts\, a Northern California pop singer-
 songwriter whose sound is steeped in the golden era of songwriting.\n\nRai
 sed on classical music\, The Beatles\, and The Beach Boys\, Callie discove
 red her calling through the great writers of the '60s and '70s—Joni Mitc
 hell\, Elton John\, Stevie Wonder\, Paul Simon\, Billy Joel\, and Carole K
 ing. These legendary artists shaped her melodic writing style and continue
  to influence every note she plays.\n\nA versatile musician\, Callie has s
 pent her career as a keyboardist\, guitarist\, writer\, arranger\, and lea
 d/backing vocalist—performing solo and with local and Bay Area bands acr
 oss multiple genres. Expect an afternoon of soulful melodies\, timeless cl
 assics\, and songs that transport you back to when music was everything.\n
 \nWhat's No Cell Sundays?\n\nIt's simple: disconnect from your devices\, r
 econnect with great wine\, live music\, and the people around you. Check y
 our phone with us at the door and receive a complimentary tasting. Bring a
  blanket\, grab a glass\, and spend your Sunday the way it was meant to be
  spent.
LOCATION:Hook & Ladder Winery
URL:https://www.hookandladderwinery.com/event/no-cell-sundays-callie-watts
 -kris-dilbeck
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
