 ctober 3\, 3 to 5pm. Meet GRO Artists\, see the show\, and enjoy a glass 
 of wine. Shows run until November 8\, open 11am to 5pm\, Thurs through Mon
 . https://galleryrouteone.org
LOCATION:Gallery Route One
URL:https://galleryrouteone.org
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Exhibit: Aspirations
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261019T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261019T180000
UID:260916itIBcRbOxUKz1YVJAgFNEg
DESCRIPTION:Date: FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE  9/15/26\n\n**OCTOBER EXHIBIT: AS
 PIRATIONS**\n\nEXHIBIT DATES **– September 28 – October 25\, 2026**\n\
 n**RECEPTION: SATURDAY\, October 3\, 2026\, 3-6 pm: Join us to meet Laura 
 Roney and Linda Loveland Reid and learn about their art and inspiration. 
  Be sure to take part in the Gallery’s free monthlong drawing for a beau
 tiful work by a Gallery artist.  Refreshments will be served.**\n\nSonoma
  County artist\, **Laura Roney\,** unveils **Aspirations**\, a new collect
 ion of paintings in oil\, celebrating the unique differing goals people se
 t during our lives\, challenging us to take bold steps forward.  Of unive
 rsal inspiration**\, Aspiration and Awe** splashes the Milky Way’s starr
 y brilliance across the heavens\, capturing our imagination and hope as wo
 rldly cares are left behind.  Moving from natural forces to human endeavo
 r\, looking toward social change\, **Aspiring to Vote**\, the portrait of 
 a hopeful suffragette\, evokes the dream for a better future.  A lifetime
  goal for many\, the marathon\, **Aspiring for 26.2\,** captures the early
  morning excitement waiting for start times.  “People doing ordinary th
 ings but dreaming larger for the future has been a great inspiration for t
 his series.  I hope folks will be inspired by the boldness of people’s 
 dreams\,” commented Roney on her inspiration for the work.\n\nArt has be
 en a lifelong passion for Roney.  Beginning her art studies at a young ag
 e\, whatever avenue she was pursuing in life\, she continued her artistic 
 endeavors.  After a successful career in microbiology and pharmaceutical 
 research\, a family move to Northern California enabled Roney to focus on 
 her art.  She received her MFA from Academy of Art University\, San Franc
 isco.\n\nMeet the artist: Roney will host the Gallery on September 30 and 
 October 1 from 11am to 6 pm.\n\nThe Stairway Smallworks Showcase features 
 Linda Loveland Reid’s **Intentional Chaos\,** a collection of exciting m
 ixed-media works that explode with excitement and energy. Random patterns\
 , amorphous shapes and dancing dribbles magically coalesce into bold state
 ments.  Intriguing and compelling\, like interlocking gears\, in **Patter
 ns of Memory** multiple patterns interlock on fields of gold and black.  
 “I love throwing ink\, paint and even coffee onto a blank canvas and cre
 ating through instinct\, gesture and emotion.  Distilling energy into sma
 ller works brings new challenges and some happy surprises\,” noted Reid 
 on her creative process.\n\nMeet the artist: Reid will host the Gallery on
  October 23 from 11am to 6 pm.\n\n Also join us for **ART NITE HEALDSBURG
 **\, Thursday\, October 1\, 5 – 7 pm.  ART NITE Healdsburg\, held the 1
 st Thursday of Every Month\, is a community event celebrating art and crea
 tivity with over 20 galleries participating.  ArtNiteHealdsburg.com.\n\nU
 pstairs Art Gallery\, 306 Center Street\, Healdsburg\, CA 95448. (707) 431
 -4214.: OPEN DAILY: 11am – 6 pm.    **www.upstairsart gallery.net** \
 n\nFor further information: Contact: Beverly Bird\, Press Contact\, at bvd
 rio@sonic.net or 707-799-1490.
LOCATION:Upstairs Art Gallery
URL:http://www.upstairsartgallery.net
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Exhibit: Aspirations
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261019T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261019T180000
UID:260916XDsk8DrxNEydzkrkm6SLOg
DESCRIPTION:Date: FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE  9/15/26\n\nOCTOBER EXHIBIT: ASPI
 RATIONS\n\nEXHIBIT DATES – September 28 – October 25\, 2026\n\nRECEPTI
 ON: SATURDAY\, October 3\, 2026\, 3-6 pm: Join us to meet Laura Roney and 
 Linda Loveland Reid and learn about their art and inspiration.  Be sure t
 o take part in the Gallery’s free monthlong drawing for a beautiful work
  by a Gallery artist.  Refreshments will be served.\n\nSonoma County arti
 st\, Laura Roney\, unveils Aspirations\, a new collection of paintings in 
 oil\, celebrating the unique differing goals people set during our lives\,
  challenging us to take bold steps forward.  Of universal inspiration\, A
 spiration and Awe splashes the Milky Way’s starry brilliance across the 
 heavens\, capturing our imagination and hope as worldly cares are left beh
 ind.  Moving from natural forces to human endeavor\, looking toward socia
 l change\, Aspiring to Vote\, the portrait of a hopeful suffragette\, evok
 es the dream for a better future.  A lifetime goal for many\, the maratho
 n\, Aspiring for 26.2\, captures the early morning excitement waiting for 
 start times.  “People doing ordinary things but dreaming larger for the
  future has been a great inspiration for this series.  I hope folks will 
 be inspired by the boldness of people’s dreams\,” commented Roney on h
 er inspiration for the work.\n\nArt has been a lifelong passion for Roney.
   Beginning her art studies at a young age\, whatever avenue she was purs
 uing in life\, she continued her artistic endeavors.  After a successful 
 career in microbiology and pharmaceutical research\, a family move to Nort
 hern California enabled Roney to focus on her art.  She received her MFA 
 from Academy of Art University\, San Francisco.\n\nMeet the artist: Roney 
 will host the Gallery on September 30 and October 1 from 11am to 6 pm.\n\n
 The Stairway Smallworks Showcase features Linda Loveland Reid’s Intentio
 nal Chaos\, a collection of exciting mixed-media works that explode with e
 xcitement and energy. Random patterns\, amorphous shapes and dancing dribb
 les magically coalesce into bold statements.  Intriguing and compelling\,
  like interlocking gears\, in Patterns of Memory multiple patterns interlo
 ck on fields of gold and black.  “I love throwing ink\, paint and even 
 coffee onto a blank canvas and creating through instinct\, gesture and emo
 tion.  Distilling energy into smaller works brings new challenges and som
 e happy surprises\,” noted Reid on her creative process.\n\nMeet the art
 ist: Reid will host the Gallery on October 23 from 11am to 6 pm.\n\n Also
  join us for ART NITE HEALDSBURG\, Thursday\, October 1\, 5 – 7 pm.  AR
 T NITE Healdsburg\, held the 1st Thursday of Every Month\, is a community 
 event celebrating art and creativity with over 20 galleries participating.
   ArtNiteHealdsburg.com.\n\nUpstairs Art Gallery\, 306 Center Street\, He
 aldsburg\, CA 95448. \\(707\\) 431-4214.: OPEN DAILY: 11am – 6 pm.   
  www.upstairsart gallery.net \n\nFor further information: Contact: Beverly
  Bird\, Press Contact\, at bvdrio@sonic.net or 707-799-1490.
LOCATION:Upstairs Art Gallery
URL:http://www.upstairsartgallery.net
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Antarctica: The Frozen Desert | Photographs by Vegar Abelsnes
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261019T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261019T170000
UID:260914CFLQ-7KWX06fJrMIXNp_bw
DESCRIPTION:1st Street Gallery at WTRSHD will present *“Antarctica: The 
 Frozen Desert\,”* a new body of fine art photography by Vegar Abelsnes\,
  opening September 26th\, 2026\, and on view September through November. 
  The exhibition marks a deliberate turn in Abelsnes’ photography\; after
  more than two decades of working in a commercial and advertising capacity
 \, he has embarked on a career as a photo and field guide in the polar reg
 ions. The exhibit features work generated over 6 *voyages to the* Antarcti
 c Peninsula. He is returning to Antarctica in January and will add the Fal
 klands and South Georgia to his list of destinations to guide and photogra
 ph.\n\nTraveling to some of the most remote and inhospitable coastlines on
  Earth\, Abelsnes has photographed a landscape that exists almost entirely
  outside of human time. The ice in these images began forming millions of 
 years ago\, while Homo sapiens have only existed for roughly 300\,000 year
 s. Defined by such a scale\, Antarctica is less a place than a record — 
 vast\, indifferent\, treacherous\, and staggeringly beautiful\, holding a 
 kind of cosmic truth that Abelsnes says is more important now than ever be
 fore.
LOCATION:1st Street Gallery @ WTRSHD
URL:https://vegarabelsnes.com/ANTARCTICA:-The-Frozen-Desert/thumbs
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:California Native Creations Art Show
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261019T083000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261019T163000
UID:260909RFf0tdAdDEu9ViMBUMbgLw
DESCRIPTION:**September is the 17th Annual Pomo Honoring Month.** On Monda
 y\, Sept. 14\, the 6th California Native Creations Art Show opens Person S
 enior Wing\, Finley Community Center\, 2060 W. College Ave.\, Santa Rosa\,
  CA. The show is free and open to the public Monday – Friday\, 8:30 a.m.
 -4:30 p.m.\, through November 19.\n\nThe established and up-and-coming nat
 ive artists create with digital media\, paint and traditional materials in
  their art\, weaving\, regalia\, beadwork\, jewelry\, baskets and quilts.
  The artists include:\n\n·         Meyo Marrufo\, painter\, gues
 t curator for the de Young Museum and the Sonoma Valley Art Museum\,\n\n·
          Buffie Campbell\, Vice Chair\, Sherwood Valley Rancheria\
 , cultural teacher and master basket maker\,\n\n·         Henry E
 dward Frank\, *Yurok/Kashaya Pomo*\, who will show paintings and work with
  Legos titled *Mind Prison\,*\n\n·         Digital artist Nicolas
  (Nico) Vargas\, *Kashia Band of Pomo Indians*\, whose art was featured at
  the 55th Annual Stanford Powwow.\n\n·         plus Gloria Carret
 ero\; Rose Hammock\; Rudy Hammock\; Jocelyn Garcia\; Arella Ortega LaRose\
 , *Kashia Band of Pomo Indians*\; Angelica Smith\, *Manchester Point Arena
  and Yokayo Rancheria*\; Maria Pasalo\; Michelle Napoli\; Martina Morgan\,
  *Kashia Band of Pomo Indians*\; Hands Lopez\; Shashoni Hanover-Redenbaug
 h\; Katie Williams-Elliott\, Juan Partida\, and Mia Pasalo\, *Big Valley P
 omo Tribe*.
LOCATION:Person Senior Wing\, Finley Community Center
URL:http://www.pomoproject.org/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Haunted Wine Tour & Tasting
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261019T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261019T173000
UID:260831mylFrEsSiEeMeHSTG3j-Ng
DESCRIPTION:This fall\, Buena Vista Winery invites you to uncover the myst
 eries\, legends\, and ghostly encounters woven into more than 165 years of
  history. Led by Sonoma historian and actor George Webber\, this immersive
  90 minute experience journeys through the historic Press House and Champa
 gne Cellars\, revealing true tales of unexplained happenings reported by B
 uena Vista team members and visitors throughout the years.\n\nHear the sto
 ries of the Glowing Ghostly Shirt\, the Little Girl Who Says Hi\, the myst
 erious Ghost Party on the Second Floor\, the Old Man Who Walked Into a Sto
 ne Wall\, and other strange occurrences that continue to add to the legend
  of Buena Vista.\n\nAlong the way\, explore some of the winery’s most in
 triguing spaces\, including the Bubble Lounge\, Cave of Curiosities\, and 
 Wine Tool Museum\, while enjoying five Buena Vista wines tasted throughout
  the experience\, including a taste drawn directly from barrel.\n\nAnd\, a
 s with any journey through Buena Vista’s extraordinary past\, you never 
 quite know when the winery’s legendary founder\, Count Agoston Haraszthy
 \, may choose to make an appearance.\n\nHistory\, wine\, mystery\, and per
 haps a spirit or two await.
LOCATION:Buena Vista Historical Winery
URL:https://eventvesta.com/events/160340/t/tickets
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Maple Magic & Winter Wonder
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261019T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261019T170000
UID:2608243oK5nEejLUW26qanwAr4yA
DESCRIPTION:As the days grow shorter and cooler\, Sonoma Botanical Garden 
 transforms with the beauty of the changing seasons. From the first signs o
 f autumn in October to the brilliant display of rare Asian maples in Nov
 ember and the quiet beauty of early winter in December\, each visit offer
 s something new to discover. \n\n*Maple Magic* *& Winter Wonder* invites
  visitors to experience this special time of year through nature\, creativ
 ity\, and connection. Throughout the season\, the Garden offers guided wal
 ks\, hands-on workshops\, lectures\, and special experiences inspired by t
 he changing landscape. Wander among vibrant fall foliage\, breathe in the 
 sweet fragrance of katsura trees\, enjoy creative programs\, and experienc
 e the peaceful beauty of the Garden as it transitions into winter.
LOCATION:Sonoma Botanical Garden
URL:https://sonomabg.org/visit/maple-magic-winter-wonder/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Harvest Tour and Tasting at Whitehall Lane Winery
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261019T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261019T110000
UID:260817CyEKAAKkp023F9ZIs3qRVQ
DESCRIPTION:We'll guide you through the winery\, show you where the wine
 making begins\, where it rests in barrel and how the product is finished\,
  while enjoying a sip each step of the way. This tour is only offered Sept
 ember through October\, Sunday - Friday at 10am and 11am while lasting\, 
 approximately 90 minutes.
LOCATION:Whitehall Lane Winery
URL:https://www.exploretock.com/whitehalllane/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
